WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:05.980
[Shinsengumi Headquarters]

00:01.410 --> 00:06.120
Did you hear? It seems that guy is returning
to Edo after finishing his job.

00:06.410 --> 00:09.610
It's Sensei, right? His baggage
arrived already.

00:10.010 --> 00:12.130
The new weapons he got are inside.

00:12.130 --> 00:15.590
I heard he also picked up some
good quality swords,

00:15.980 --> 00:18.300
so the top members are scrambling.

00:18.300 --> 00:21.600
They're really lucky.
I want a new sword, too.

00:21.600 --> 00:23.380
Ah-hem.

00:23.970 --> 00:25.580
Ah, Yamazaki-san.

00:26.030 --> 00:28.810
Ah! Could that sword be...

00:28.810 --> 00:30.420
...an Osafune Mark II?!

00:28.810 --> 00:30.420
[Note: Parody of Bizen Osafune, a famous sword.]

00:30.420 --> 00:32.950
That's great! It's got the brand
name on it. So cool!

00:32.950 --> 00:35.910
Well, it's not like I came
here to show it off.

00:35.910 --> 00:38.530
I just happened to pass by. By chance...

00:38.530 --> 00:39.520
I'm jealous.

00:39.520 --> 00:42.070
Just a little... Please let
me try a practice swing!

00:42.070 --> 00:43.790
Ah, of course you can.

00:44.560 --> 00:47.530
Wow! I can really feel that
brand-name difference!

00:47.530 --> 00:52.870
Additionally, it's waterproof. I don't
want to brag, you know...

00:52.870 --> 00:56.000
Hey, what are you guys making
such a fuss about?

00:56.000 --> 00:57.420
Ah, Captain Okita.

00:57.420 --> 00:59.520
Look at Yamazaki-san's sword...

00:59.890 --> 01:00.540
Huh?

01:01.470 --> 01:02.870
That sword is a...

01:02.870 --> 01:05.710
Kikuichimonji RX-78!

01:02.870 --> 01:05.710
[Note: It's rumored the historical Soji Okita
used a sword named Kikuichimonji.]

01:05.710 --> 01:11.970
It has a built-in digital music player with
a maximum playing time of 124 hours!

01:11.970 --> 01:13.920
It's the Kikuichimonji RX-78!

01:13.920 --> 01:16.090
It costs twice as much as the Osafune!

01:16.090 --> 01:19.630
The swords at the captain's
level are really something!

01:19.630 --> 01:21.510
Hmm... Is this sword that great?

01:21.510 --> 01:24.100
I just picked it up without thinking,
so I didn't realize that.

01:24.540 --> 01:25.550
Huh?

01:25.550 --> 01:27.700
What's that stick? Yamazaki... What
is that? Did you buy that?

01:27.700 --> 01:29.140
It almost looks rusted.

01:29.540 --> 01:32.120
Captain, please let me try a
few practice swings for a bit!

01:33.180 --> 01:36.120
Wow! This first-class stuff
is really amazing!

01:36.120 --> 01:39.220
It sounds completely different!
The deep bass is amazing!

01:39.650 --> 01:42.140
Hey, what's going on? Why
is it so noisy this morning?

01:42.280 --> 01:44.400
Chief! I'm sorry. Well...

01:44.600 --> 01:46.030
That sword is...

01:46.030 --> 01:48.370
The Kotetsu Z-Second.

01:46.030 --> 01:48.370
[Note: Kotetsu Nagasone was a famous swordsmith. The historical Isami Kondo was said to own a fake Kotetsu sword.]

01:48.370 --> 01:50.600
Not only does it have digital
music equipment,

01:50.600 --> 01:55.680
but it also has a special metal attachment on
the end that can be used as a floor cleaner!

01:56.330 --> 01:59.580
It costs three times as much
as the Kikuichimonji! Cool!

01:59.840 --> 02:05.110
You guys are using such cheap swords?
A sword is a samurai's soul.

02:05.110 --> 02:09.010
If you use such shabby swords, it'll
reveal the true nature of your soul.

02:09.010 --> 02:11.810
Kondo-san, you're great! We
won't ever be equal to you.

02:11.810 --> 02:15.320
We should work harder and hope to some
day own stuff on your kind of level.

02:15.770 --> 02:19.530
Kondo-san, can I try some practice
swings for a moment?

02:19.530 --> 02:21.410
Ah, go right ahead.

02:22.210 --> 02:23.780
There!

02:23.780 --> 02:25.670
Kotetsu!

02:25.670 --> 02:30.250
Ah, I'm sorry. I thought a sword like this
could cut through rock, but it failed.

02:30.250 --> 02:32.250
You! You definitely did that on purpose!

02:32.250 --> 02:35.250
You were jealous of my Kotetsu-chan...
You were jealous!

02:35.850 --> 02:39.770
I'm not going to say a sword
is a samurai's soul.

02:39.980 --> 02:45.500
Besides, I don't think the level of the
sword one carries raises his status.

02:45.920 --> 02:48.510
For me, a sword is just a sword.

02:48.780 --> 02:52.880
And that's the most important
thing to me.

02:53.510 --> 02:58.760
Most important of all is a sword that can
break through the enemy's blade.

02:59.480 --> 03:02.220
It seems you're overdoing
it as rashly as ever.

03:02.220 --> 03:05.120
A sword can be used again
after it's been mended,

03:05.120 --> 03:06.730
but humans don't work that way.

03:07.290 --> 03:10.470
As long as a human doesn't
break, he can recover, right?

03:10.470 --> 03:14.550
If you keep fighting in such a way that
damages your sword so much,

03:14.550 --> 03:18.270
you'll end up being broken in two
pretty soon. That's what I meant.

03:20.150 --> 03:22.140
This looks like a good sword.

03:22.640 --> 03:26.610
Old man, until mine is repaired,
let me borrow this.

03:26.610 --> 03:27.860
You can't use that one.

03:28.940 --> 03:32.000
That sword comes with a story behind it.

03:32.000 --> 03:36.200
What? You mean I can listen to music with
it or it can be used as a floor cleaner?

03:36.200 --> 03:40.060
There's no question that sword
is terribly sharp. However...

03:41.730 --> 03:43.060
It's cursed.

03:44.140 --> 03:46.490
Cursed? You've got to be kidding me.

03:47.070 --> 03:52.800
An ordinary sword user will be consumed
by the soul of that sword.

03:52.800 --> 03:54.650
You won't able to handle it.

03:54.650 --> 03:58.950
...Will you listen to my old
story for a moment?

03:58.950 --> 04:03.050
It's a tragic tale of a reincarnated
demonic sword...

04:04.310 --> 04:05.720
But I didn't listen to it.

04:06.300 --> 04:11.090
In general, old men's stories tend to
be long. I don't have time for that.

04:11.730 --> 04:15.460
Whether its price is high or low, whether
it can be used to listen to music,

04:15.790 --> 04:19.470
or whether the sword is cursed,
it doesn't matter to me.

04:21.120 --> 04:25.340
You must be Shinsengumi Vice-Chief
Toshiro Hijikata-dono.

04:25.340 --> 04:28.220
Although you're a samurai, you've
sided with the Amanto for perks!

04:28.220 --> 04:30.420
You're a traitor! We, the advanced
party of the Anti-Foreigner Faction,

04:30.420 --> 04:32.950
are here to bring punishment
from heaven!

04:33.950 --> 04:36.570
This is a chance to test it out.

04:36.570 --> 04:38.880
Let me see how this cursed
demonic sword works.

04:40.410 --> 04:42.920
Here we go!

04:43.210 --> 04:45.420
I'm sorry!

04:51.360 --> 04:53.430
Huh? What's this...?

04:53.760 --> 04:57.440
Wh-What am I doing? My body
is moving on its own...

04:57.680 --> 04:59.270
My mouth is moving on its own...

04:59.270 --> 05:04.000
I'm sorry! My life! Please spare me!

05:04.000 --> 05:06.450
I'll lick anything, even the
soles of your sandals!

05:08.630 --> 05:11.180
Who's this pathetic guy?!

05:11.180 --> 05:12.950
That's Toshiro Hijikata!

05:12.950 --> 05:16.710
The man who is feared as the Demon
Vice-Chief! How miserable!

05:17.910 --> 05:22.480
Wh-Wh-What's wrong with me?!
My body doesn't respond at all!

05:22.480 --> 05:27.670
An ordinary sword user will be consumed
by the soul of that sword.

05:28.600 --> 05:30.500
Don't tell me... This...?!

05:30.500 --> 05:36.000
Why is the demonic sword's curse making
me act this way?! That's ridiculous...!

05:36.980 --> 05:38.870
I don't know what's going on,

05:38.870 --> 05:43.480
but we'll be paying you back for
everything you did to us before!

05:44.970 --> 05:47.330
You just said you would lick the soles
of our sandals, didn't you?!

05:47.330 --> 05:49.140
Then lick it!

05:49.140 --> 05:51.990
Y-You bastard!

05:55.130 --> 06:02.100
It may be a cursed sword or whatever,
but... I... Ugh... won't...!

06:02.950 --> 06:06.290
Um... Please forgive
me by accepting this.

06:06.290 --> 06:07.570
I have 3,000 yen.

06:07.890 --> 06:10.740
But please don't take my Suica, because
I won't be able to go home without it.

06:08.390 --> 06:11.240
[Note: Suica is a rechargeable IC card used
as a fare card on train lines in Japan.]

06:11.240 --> 06:12.800
Don't screw with us!

06:12.800 --> 06:15.250
What's with this guy?!
He's flip-flopping his personality!

06:15.250 --> 06:19.000
Anyway, why does an adult like
you have only 3,000 yen?!

06:19.000 --> 06:21.650
This is bad... There's something
totally wrong with me...

06:22.060 --> 06:23.510
I'm a goner...

06:24.080 --> 06:25.730
As things are...

06:25.730 --> 06:26.980
I'll be finished...

06:27.360 --> 06:28.230
Hey!

06:36.010 --> 06:37.390
A familiar uniform.

06:37.390 --> 06:39.120
A familiar stance.

06:39.120 --> 06:41.380
But his face is...

06:47.320 --> 06:51.950
I just saw a member of the Shinsengumi
being attacked, so I rushed over here...

06:52.300 --> 06:55.190
What are you doing in a place like this,

06:55.660 --> 06:57.310
Hijikata-kun?

06:57.760 --> 06:59.150
You're...

07:05.550 --> 07:09.520
A toast to Kamotaro Ito-kun's
return. Cheers!

07:09.520 --> 07:11.530
Cheers!

07:14.400 --> 07:18.900
Well, Ito Sensei, you did
a good job this time.

07:18.900 --> 07:20.570
But that many weapons...

07:20.570 --> 07:24.500
I wonder how you got those stingy people in
the government to loosen their purse strings!

07:24.500 --> 07:29.690
Kondo-san, being stingy means being shrewd
enough to profit from a different viewpoint.

07:29.890 --> 07:34.870
All you have to do is just explain that the government
will profit by making expenditures on us...

07:37.430 --> 07:40.560
Though, just as you say, Kondo-san,

07:40.790 --> 07:45.850
they're pertinacious people who don't care
about our hardships and groveling.

07:46.510 --> 07:52.010
It wasn't easy for me to explain it to them,
in a way they could easily understand.

07:53.930 --> 07:56.030
That's right! That's absolutely right!

07:56.030 --> 07:58.690
They're pertinacious! They really are!

07:58.690 --> 08:00.740
Kondo-san, what does
pertinacious mean?

08:00.740 --> 08:03.170
You shut up! Kids should be quiet!

08:04.270 --> 08:09.200
Kondo-san, if people like them stay at
the top, this country will be ruined.

08:09.710 --> 08:13.280
We can't stay in a smoldering
place like this.

08:14.040 --> 08:18.600
We have to move forward! We must
work toward a higher goal!

08:19.020 --> 08:24.730
And we'll eventually become like the swords,
the keystones of this country.

08:24.730 --> 08:27.840
I believe that saving this confused country is
the mission for those of us born as samurai.

08:28.360 --> 08:32.670
For that, I wouldn't mind
giving my life to you!

08:33.330 --> 08:35.730
Kondo-san, let's work hard together!

08:36.030 --> 08:39.000
Right. Everyone, let's work
hard pertinacious!

08:39.000 --> 08:41.370
No, you're using "pertinacious"
the wrong way.

08:43.380 --> 08:46.880
Ito-san has started expressing
his valuable opinions again.

08:46.880 --> 08:49.910
Even the Chief calls him "Sensei."

08:49.910 --> 08:52.380
He's just a newcomer who
joined us only a year ago.

08:52.380 --> 08:55.600
I wonder if he's getting so full of himself

08:55.600 --> 08:57.190
because he was just assigned the title of advisor.

08:57.390 --> 08:58.990
I'm not blaming him.

08:58.990 --> 09:03.780
He's intelligent, really good at his job and
is fully proficient in Hokuto Itto Ryu.

08:58.990 --> 09:03.780
[Note: The Hokuto Itto Ryu is a northern sword style.]

09:04.430 --> 09:09.330
Vice-Chief is also intelligent, but he's
really only a battle strategist.

09:09.330 --> 09:11.940
So Ito-san's the only person who
can manage political matters.

09:11.940 --> 09:14.570
No wonder he is a great help to the chief.

09:14.570 --> 09:20.040
Ito-san has hardly ever been in the headquarters...
but it might be about time...

09:20.490 --> 09:21.420
For what?

09:21.460 --> 09:26.470
I've never seen Ito-san and Hijikata-san talk
about each other, only about their jobs.

09:38.240 --> 09:41.750
Hijikata-kun, I have something
to ask you.

09:41.750 --> 09:43.910
What a coincidence... me, too.

09:44.990 --> 09:47.440
You hate me,
don't you?

09:44.990 --> 09:47.440
You hate me,
don't you?

09:47.880 --> 09:51.280
Because I'm Kondo-san's favorite,
and although I'm a newcomer,

09:51.280 --> 09:54.460
I'm rising to fame so fast
that it threatens you.

09:54.890 --> 09:56.970
I bet I'm an eyesore to you, right?

09:57.710 --> 10:03.500
That's what you think? You want to advance
in your career, but I'm higher than you.

10:03.750 --> 10:06.240
I bet I'm an eyesore to you, right?

10:07.510 --> 10:12.280
It's a groundless suspicion, Hijikata-kun.
I don't think about that kind of thing.

10:12.280 --> 10:15.220
That's good. It seems we have cleared
up any misunderstandings.

10:15.480 --> 10:17.350
An eyesore...

10:17.350 --> 10:19.850
It's even more than that.

10:20.650 --> 10:22.910
Some time in the future, I'll kill you.

10:24.540 --> 10:25.560
Toshi...

10:26.010 --> 10:27.930
I heard about you from Ito Sensei.

10:28.160 --> 10:31.540
That was a stroke of bad
luck. How's your injury?

10:33.440 --> 10:34.490
Toshi...

10:34.880 --> 10:38.100
Although we call ourselves samurai,

10:38.100 --> 10:40.410
we're really just a bunch of country boys.

10:40.490 --> 10:51.790
[Kyukuchu Hatto]

10:40.960 --> 10:43.460
Even though that's what we
are, when facing death,

10:43.460 --> 10:46.440
we're able to act more like
samurai than real samurai.

10:46.670 --> 10:49.000
It was because of the Kyokuchu Hatto,

10:49.000 --> 10:51.240
the strict laws you created,
that we can be like that.

10:51.890 --> 10:56.110
It has 45 articles, encompassing everything
from daily behavior to manners,

10:56.110 --> 10:57.940
and even battle preparation.

10:57.940 --> 11:00.040
These are the strict laws that govern us.

11:00.040 --> 11:02.450
If you break any one of those laws,
you'll have to commit seppuku.

11:02.830 --> 11:06.630
That's your image of the ideal samurai.

11:07.130 --> 11:09.350
We all agree.

11:09.620 --> 11:11.030
Do you understand, Toshi?

11:11.030 --> 11:14.090
You're the ideal samurai
model for everyone.

11:14.730 --> 11:18.310
Everyone models himself after
you. Everyone watches you.

11:18.920 --> 11:23.550
I'm not in a position to say this, but don't do
anything to betray the way of the samurai.

11:24.220 --> 11:26.170
...He's quite a guy.

11:26.590 --> 11:30.320
As quick as a flash, news of my
shameful behavior has spread.

11:30.320 --> 11:36.470
Well, for him, it's the perfect opportunity
to defeat me and rise up the ladder.

11:36.470 --> 11:41.060
Toshi, stop talking that way. Ito Sensei is
thinking about the spirit of the group...

11:41.060 --> 11:44.090
I already told you to stop
calling him "Sensei."

11:44.090 --> 11:48.690
Kondo-san, are you going to give
your position of Chief to him?

11:48.690 --> 11:49.510
If that's not the case,

11:49.510 --> 11:53.470
are you going to share your position as
head of the Shinsengumi with him?

11:54.200 --> 11:58.120
Need I remind you that members are
unsure about how to treat him.

11:58.960 --> 12:04.930
His former colleagues, who entered at
the same time, are already his allies.

12:05.200 --> 12:09.580
Are you saying that Ito Sensei is trying
to take over the Shinsengumi?

12:09.580 --> 12:10.390
Who knows?

12:10.390 --> 12:14.880
But ever since he got here he's done nothing
but gather allies and influence.

12:14.880 --> 12:17.950
...It's obvious he's up to something.

12:17.950 --> 12:22.880
He's not as powerful as he wants
to be and he's not satisfied.

12:23.930 --> 12:27.380
Kondo-san... If a snake has two heads...

12:27.380 --> 12:34.250
...one either has to rot and fall off or the
ensuing feud will split the body in two.

12:35.200 --> 12:39.560
I believe that Ito Sensei is a crucial
man for the Shinsengumi.

12:40.830 --> 12:45.350
Hey, Toshi, we're not doing this
to ensure your own position.

12:45.750 --> 12:49.050
We're doing this to protect Edo and
to stick to the ways of the samurai.

12:49.340 --> 12:52.540
To get that wisdom, I'll ask for
anyone who can teach it.

12:52.890 --> 12:56.710
It's natural to call the person
who teaches us "Sensei."

12:57.160 --> 13:00.450
If you ask me to treat him
like a follower, I'll refuse.

13:01.090 --> 13:04.000
I've never thought of you
guys as my followers.

13:05.080 --> 13:08.480
As for the way of the samurai,
we're on equal footing.

13:10.510 --> 13:14.470
Kondo-san, you don't
understand anything.

13:14.470 --> 13:16.840
Pretty words won't help manage
the organization...!

13:19.750 --> 13:20.940
Toshi!

13:23.910 --> 13:28.050
Pretty Girl Samurai, Tomoe 5000 is here!

13:24.210 --> 13:28.050
[Note: Parody of Sailor Moon]

13:28.050 --> 13:34.440
Damn it! It's already started! I forgot
to record it! Tomoe-chan!

13:35.260 --> 13:37.100
My body...again...

13:37.960 --> 13:40.420
What am I watching?!

13:44.520 --> 13:46.440
Punishment is complete.

13:47.630 --> 13:50.220
Hey, hey, did you hear
about the Vice-Chief?

13:50.220 --> 13:51.040
Hear what?

13:51.040 --> 13:54.670
The Vice-Chief was attacked by Anti-Foreigner
Faction ronin the other day.

13:54.670 --> 13:58.310
He was saved by Ito-san. But
you probably won't believe it.

13:58.600 --> 14:02.250
The Vice-Chief knelt, bowed
and begged for his life.

14:02.250 --> 14:04.450
It's impossible that something
like that could happen.

14:04.450 --> 14:07.420
He would rather die than
do something like that.

14:07.420 --> 14:09.320
He's the demon Vice-Chief.
The "demon."

14:09.320 --> 14:11.010
But I heard it, too.

14:11.010 --> 14:13.070
Hey, hey, cut it out already.

14:13.070 --> 14:15.500
If this conversation is overheard,
we'll be in trouble.

14:15.500 --> 14:19.230
It's against the Kyokuchu Hatto
rules to pass JUMP around.

14:19.230 --> 14:22.800
"No reading of manga, except for MAGAZINE,
allowed in the headquarters."

14:19.230 --> 14:22.800
[Note: MAGAZINE refers to "Weekly Shonen
MAGAZINE, a rival of Shonen JUMP.]

14:22.800 --> 14:24.970
If someone sees us, we'll
have to commit seppuku.

14:24.970 --> 14:26.900
Hijikata prefers MAGAZINE.

14:26.900 --> 14:27.830
Let me see that.

14:27.830 --> 14:31.900
Moreover, he liked yankee manga a decade
ago. It's hard for us JUMP fans.

14:27.830 --> 14:31.900
[Note: Yankee manga is a genre
where bad boys fight others.]

14:32.980 --> 14:35.990
V-Vice-Chief! Wh-When did you...?!

14:35.990 --> 14:38.160
No, that's like nothing... That's...uh!

14:38.160 --> 14:41.340
The thickness of the book is about the
same...so I bought it by mistake!

14:41.340 --> 14:42.390
Hey!

14:42.390 --> 14:43.340
Yes, sir!

14:43.340 --> 14:45.940
"To Love-Ru" is super interesting !

14:43.340 --> 14:45.940
[Note: "ToLoveる" is a manga in JUMP.]

14:47.640 --> 14:49.490
I'm going to buy the manga.

14:50.100 --> 14:52.800
"To-To-To Love-Ru?" Is
that the Vice-Chief?!

14:52.800 --> 14:55.250
For argument's sake, "Boys be…"

14:52.800 --> 14:55.250
[Note: "Boys be…" is a manga in
Weekly Shonen MAGAZINE.]

14:55.680 --> 14:59.170
[MEETING ROOM]

14:56.290 --> 14:59.170
These days, attacks by Anti-Foreigner
Faction ronin have increased.

14:59.170 --> 15:02.280
So, make sure not to go off on your own.

15:02.280 --> 15:03.560
Yes, sir!

15:03.560 --> 15:06.530
Then, I'll assign today's
shift. Squad one is…

15:08.150 --> 15:09.630
Damn it! My cell phone...!

15:09.630 --> 15:10.730
You idiot!

15:10.730 --> 15:12.440
If your cell phone rings during a meeting,

15:12.440 --> 15:13.950
you'll have to commit seppuku
according to the Kyukuchu Hatto.

15:14.900 --> 15:19.460
Hijikata-san! Nothing… I… My wife
is in labor, so she called me…

15:19.460 --> 15:29.070
[Note: The Pretty Cure (a magical
girl series) song is playing.]

15:30.100 --> 15:31.830
Hello, this is Hijikata…

15:33.390 --> 15:36.050
Yes…right now? No problem.

15:36.810 --> 15:41.220
Huh? The limited-edition DVD
BOX comes with a figurine?

15:41.580 --> 15:44.850
Well, then…one to save, and one for
that… I'll need a total of two sets.

15:50.260 --> 15:55.280
Hey! Spit it out! I'm asking you
where your headquarters is!

15:55.280 --> 15:58.260
I won't sell out my own
comrades! Kill me!

15:58.260 --> 16:01.400
I'd rather die like a samurai
than shame myself!

16:01.400 --> 16:05.230
Hey, hey! Do you really think you
can die in a place like this?

16:06.770 --> 16:12.190
We'll make you feel like you’re in a
hell worse than death from now on.

16:12.190 --> 16:13.330
Vice-Chief!

16:13.330 --> 16:15.850
Work him over! Please.

16:17.200 --> 16:19.210
Get out of here, you guys.

16:19.560 --> 16:21.010
Y-Yes.

16:23.680 --> 16:26.150
He's a really scary guy…

16:26.150 --> 16:29.340
When the Vice-Chief works a
guy over with his own hands,

16:29.340 --> 16:31.630
the interrogation room becomes
completely silent.

16:32.350 --> 16:34.240
However, five minutes later,

16:34.240 --> 16:39.160
even the bravest men start crying
and spit out everything.

16:42.340 --> 16:45.300
Wh-What's going on inside?

16:45.300 --> 16:49.200
Just take a peek. You'll see hell on earth.

16:51.630 --> 16:54.230
What? Is there anyone you like?

16:54.230 --> 16:56.380
Not really. I don't have anyone.

16:56.380 --> 17:00.190
Come on! I already told you,
so it’s your turn to tell me.

17:00.190 --> 17:04.790
It's not fair! Not fair! You lied to me,
didn't you?! You did! You tell me!

17:04.790 --> 17:09.630
All right! I'll tell you then! But don't
tell anyone! It's a secret.

17:09.630 --> 17:11.810
Well, I don't know about that.

17:11.810 --> 17:15.100
Oh, damn it! The teachers are on
patrol. Put out the cigarettes!

17:15.570 --> 17:17.060
Is this a school trip or something?

17:17.990 --> 17:19.360
…That's how it goes.

17:19.990 --> 17:22.990
After I got this sword,
everything went wrong.

17:23.500 --> 17:26.850
It looks like I’m really cursed.

17:27.950 --> 17:30.140
That’s why I didn't want to tell you.

17:30.140 --> 17:33.480
You don't believe me, do you?
There's no way you'll believe me.

17:33.830 --> 17:37.070
Just like that, I had switched personalities
with someone completely different.

17:37.290 --> 17:40.390
No, that wasn't someone else.

17:40.390 --> 17:44.860
The weak side inside everyone
gets awakened by this sword.

17:45.690 --> 17:49.800
Hijikata-san, you can't blame
being weak on the sword.

17:49.800 --> 17:52.120
You were weak to begin
with, Hijikata-san.

17:52.120 --> 17:55.180
That's right; I'm always like this…

17:55.180 --> 17:58.160
Oh, my…this is really something strange.

17:58.420 --> 18:01.810
Then why don't you just throw
away that cursed sword?

18:01.810 --> 18:08.170
I would, If I could. I even find myself carrying
it with me to the toilet and bath.

18:08.170 --> 18:10.400
I can't get rid of it, even if I want to.

18:10.400 --> 18:13.820
And the old man at the swordsmith’s
isn't there anymore.

18:14.090 --> 18:18.820
Then are you trying to say…that's the reason
you had a fight with Kondo-san?

18:19.790 --> 18:21.550
…I wish I could say that…

18:21.830 --> 18:25.210
Hijikata-san, if you don’t
pay attention this time,

18:25.210 --> 18:27.650
Ito-san will take away your
vice-chief position.

18:28.360 --> 18:29.830
No time for that now.

18:30.220 --> 18:34.450
Since I became like this, I've already broken
more than ten of the Kyokuchu Hatto rules.

18:35.340 --> 18:39.420
If Ito delivers a sentence for seppuku
tomorrow, I wouldn't be surprised.

18:39.760 --> 18:42.370
As I am right now, I wouldn't refuse.

18:42.850 --> 18:46.470
If you're with me, you'll
attract Ito's attention.

18:48.370 --> 18:49.850
…Hijikata-san…

18:49.850 --> 18:51.960
Wait, Hijikata-san!

18:53.560 --> 18:56.410
Go buy me a Yakisoba pan.

18:53.560 --> 18:56.410
[Note: Yakisoba pan is noodles in a hot dog bun.]

18:56.410 --> 18:59.410
And JUMP, too. Of course,
you pay for them.

19:01.620 --> 19:05.700
Toshi is late. It's already past the time.

19:06.370 --> 19:08.350
This is a really important meeting…

19:08.780 --> 19:09.950
Kondo-san.

19:10.270 --> 19:15.360
This is a good opportunity. I was going
to bring him up for discussion.

19:15.650 --> 19:19.980
I think you’ve already heard
about his recent behavior.

19:20.370 --> 19:24.700
He broke the Kyokuchu Hatto
rules more than ten times.

19:24.700 --> 19:27.390
And yet he created those
rules for the members.

19:27.610 --> 19:31.510
Besides him being late for an
important meeting like this,

19:31.880 --> 19:35.680
If we continue to let him act like this, we won't
be able to control the other members.

19:35.680 --> 19:37.930
Sensei, hold on. I know Toshi well.

19:37.930 --> 19:39.590
He must have something
exceedingly important…

19:39.590 --> 19:42.520
I'm not only talking about
this particular case.

19:42.870 --> 19:49.550
Of course, I fully understand what he
achieved for the Shinsengumi before.

19:50.100 --> 19:52.480
That's why I want to give
him some candid advice.

19:52.880 --> 19:56.600
If he's the symbol of the Shinsengumi,
and he downplays the rules,

19:56.600 --> 19:58.890
other members will do the same.

19:58.890 --> 20:01.930
A pack of wolves that has lost its discipline
will be like sheep without a shepherd.

20:02.510 --> 20:05.340
He's the one who deserves
strict punishment!

20:05.560 --> 20:07.500
Kondo-san, please make a firm decision!

20:07.500 --> 20:09.520
Hold on! Toshi will definitely…

20:13.970 --> 20:17.760
Hi! I bought your Yakisoba
pan, Okita Senpai!

20:17.760 --> 20:20.290
I'm sorry, but they didn't have
JUMP, so I got MAGAZINE…

20:34.290 --> 20:39.110
D-Damn it! I was trapped!

20:42.300 --> 20:45.390
Those guys…were working together!

20:47.650 --> 20:49.900
The NEET problem, the
hikikomori problem...

20:49.900 --> 20:52.920
The number of apathetic young
people is steadily on the rise.

20:53.560 --> 20:57.200
The people known as "Otaku" are said to
be NEETs and hikikomori in the making.

20:57.200 --> 21:00.590
Today we have gathered one hundred
self-proclaimed otaku.

21:00.800 --> 21:05.090
What do they think when they withdraw
into their inner world?

21:05.090 --> 21:07.100
We will find out what they're really like!!

21:07.100 --> 21:09.340
Otaku Summit: A Live
Debate Till Morning!

21:08.070 --> 21:10.970
[Note: Spoof of Japanese TV discussion
program "Asa Made Nama TV."]

21:09.340 --> 21:11.220
As usual, we'll be going on until morning.

21:11.220 --> 21:14.070
Oh no! It's started...

21:14.070 --> 21:16.000
Huh? This is odd...

21:16.000 --> 21:17.470
What are you doing?

21:17.470 --> 21:20.240
I've got to tape Shinpachi's gallantry.

21:20.240 --> 21:21.340
Shinpachi?

21:21.970 --> 21:24.440
Come to think of it,
he hasn't come over today.

21:24.440 --> 21:25.720
First off...

21:25.720 --> 21:31.500
I'd like to correct the notion that all otaku
are hikikomori and NEETs in the making.

21:31.620 --> 21:37.460
[53 Idol Otaku - Captain Shimura]

21:32.250 --> 21:37.460
There are otaku amongst us who
work and function in society.

21:39.450 --> 21:41.710
What is he doing?

21:41.710 --> 21:43.180
Ah, I see...

21:43.180 --> 21:44.280
Umm...

21:44.280 --> 21:46.200
Number 31, what's your opinion?

21:46.200 --> 21:47.330
Well...

21:47.330 --> 21:53.080
This show attempts to criticize and blame otaku
for causing Japan's current problems...

21:53.080 --> 21:55.230
All right, all right.

21:55.230 --> 21:58.060
I just want to get other people's
opinions, too...

21:55.230 --> 21:57.940
What's this? He's become
a really annoying guy!

21:58.060 --> 22:00.310
I'm sure the viewers definitely hate him!

22:00.310 --> 22:04.190
First off, it's weird to group
all otaku into one category!

22:04.190 --> 22:08.690
Oh no, it's getting heated! Come
on, where is that piece of junk?!

22:04.650 --> 22:08.030
Now, now... A-Anyway, sit down, okay?

22:09.070 --> 22:13.980
We're supporting a pop idol,
something that's real.

22:13.980 --> 22:15.700
But what I don't understand is...

22:15.700 --> 22:19.860
People who are in love with two-dimensional
girls from anime and games.

22:20.700 --> 22:23.610
Hey! What do you mean
by that, Number 53?!

22:23.610 --> 22:27.280
A two-dimensional girl can never be attained
even if you're in love with her.

22:27.280 --> 22:28.280
It's a waste of time.

22:28.280 --> 22:31.680
No way! Shiori-chan is alive in my heart!

22:31.680 --> 22:35.250
Oh, I have an objection. May I speak?

22:35.250 --> 22:36.360
Go right ahead.

22:36.420 --> 22:41.890
[7 Anime Otaku - Toshi]

22:36.440 --> 22:38.980
Umm... In short, Number
53 is trying to say

22:39.160 --> 22:44.400
that three-dimensional otaku are more realistic
than us two-dimensional otaku.

22:44.900 --> 22:46.960
But let me ask you this...

22:46.960 --> 22:51.600
Do you think supporting a pop idol
will help you get one to marry you?

22:52.360 --> 22:53.500
Well...

22:53.970 --> 22:55.430
You can't, can you?

22:55.430 --> 22:58.660
In other words, us two-dimensional otaku
and you three-dimensional otaku

22:58.660 --> 23:01.530
are both in love with something unattainable.

23:01.530 --> 23:02.830
We're in the same boat.

23:02.830 --> 23:05.190
No, no, you're wrong!

23:05.190 --> 23:10.860
Indeed, it's impossible to marry a pop idol.
But it's not 100 percent guaranteed.

23:11.040 --> 23:12.850
It's 100 percent impossible for you.

23:12.850 --> 23:15.330
No, it's definitely impossible for you.

23:15.330 --> 23:18.520
No, it's not! That's because
pop stars exist in real life.

23:18.520 --> 23:21.720
No, thinking about things beyond
your grasp like that

23:21.720 --> 23:25.090
is absolute proof that you're
not being realistic.

23:22.840 --> 23:24.990
<i>Number 7 sure is annoying.</i>

23:25.090 --> 23:26.840
Go, Shinpachi!!

23:26.840 --> 23:29.650
How dare you talk to
our captain like that?!

23:29.650 --> 23:30.570
What did you say?!

23:30.570 --> 23:34.570
Whoa! The two-dimensional fans and the three-dimensional
fans have begun fighting each other.

23:35.350 --> 23:36.710
It's done.

23:36.710 --> 23:38.520
It's nicely melted!!

23:38.520 --> 23:40.170
You were toasting bread?

23:40.170 --> 23:41.760
Weren't you supposed to be taping this?

23:43.050 --> 23:44.620
Huh? That guy...

23:45.400 --> 23:47.630
I've seen him somewhere...

23:47.720 --> 23:50.720
[Shinsengumi Headquarters]

23:48.050 --> 23:50.720
Hey, did you hear what happened
to Hijikata-san?

23:51.340 --> 23:53.640
He was placed under suspension
indefinitely.

23:53.640 --> 23:57.730
He broke one of the Kyukuchu Hatto.
Ito-san insisted that he commit seppuku.

23:57.730 --> 24:01.340
But the Chief and everyone else
persuaded him otherwise.

24:01.340 --> 24:06.740
He's really being forced out, isn't he?
He probably won't be coming back.

24:06.740 --> 24:11.410
Ito won't forgive him. Those two were
always at each other's throats.

24:11.410 --> 24:13.750
It's finally his time to shine, huh?

24:13.940 --> 24:17.250
According to rumors, Okita-san
has sided with Ito's faction.

24:17.250 --> 24:19.750
No one can oppose Ito anymore.

24:21.580 --> 24:23.250
How unexpected.

24:23.250 --> 24:26.760
Okita-kun, I never expected you
to come over to my side.

24:27.290 --> 24:31.570
I heard that you two knew each other
before the Shinsengumi was formed.

24:31.570 --> 24:34.770
I completely thought that you
were part of Hijikata's faction.

24:34.970 --> 24:36.270
Hijikata's faction?

24:36.930 --> 24:40.690
I wasn't aware that such
a faction ever existed.

24:41.200 --> 24:42.780
You're a smart man.

24:43.610 --> 24:45.310
What do you want?

24:46.050 --> 24:47.710
Naturally...

24:47.710 --> 24:49.550
the Vice-Chief position.

24:52.110 --> 24:54.690
As long as you stick with
me, I promise to

24:54.690 --> 24:56.640
grant you that wish.

24:58.620 --> 24:59.920
Is that all right?

24:59.920 --> 25:01.180
It doesn't matter.

25:01.180 --> 25:03.430
I'll give him the position of Vice-Chief.

25:03.430 --> 25:06.650
But if you do that, it'll defeat the
purpose of getting rid of Hijikata.

25:06.650 --> 25:07.940
Shinohara-kun...

25:07.940 --> 25:12.270
Do you think I've started this silly
power struggle with that man

25:12.270 --> 25:16.870
just so I could become Vice-Chief?

25:17.350 --> 25:19.850
[Odd Jobs Gin]

25:17.710 --> 25:20.370
Umm... I'm sorry.

25:20.370 --> 25:24.270
I never expected you to be there...

25:24.270 --> 25:25.930
H-Hijikata-san.

25:25.930 --> 25:27.330
No, it's all right.

25:27.330 --> 25:29.360
I'm just glad my limited-edition figurine...

25:29.710 --> 25:32.760
Tomoe 5000 is safe.

25:33.330 --> 25:35.270
Th-Thank you very much.

25:37.830 --> 25:42.870
Umm... What? Are you
really Hijikata-san?

25:43.420 --> 25:45.580
What are you saying, Mr. Sakata?

25:43.420 --> 25:45.580
[Note: Otaku often call each other by their
last names and the suffix "shi"  (Mr./Ms.)]

25:45.580 --> 25:46.780
"Mr. Sakata"?

25:46.780 --> 25:48.340
As you can see...

25:48.340 --> 25:51.360
I am the real Toshiro Hijikata de gozaru.

25:48.340 --> 25:52.310
[Shogunate Special Armed Police, Shinsengumi
Vice-Chief Toshiro Hijikata]

25:51.360 --> 25:52.310
"Gozaru"?

25:52.530 --> 25:53.910
Oh, Miss Kagura...

25:53.910 --> 25:55.530
That Chinese outfit!

25:56.010 --> 26:00.420
Are you dressed up as Magical
Girl Chinese Papaya?

25:56.010 --> 26:00.420
[Note: Refers to "Maho Shojo Chukana Paipai."
A live action girly series from the late 80's.]

26:00.420 --> 26:04.060
That's incredibly accurate.
Could I take your picture?

26:07.130 --> 26:08.670
Nice. That's good. One more.

26:09.640 --> 26:11.070
Why are you bashful?

26:11.680 --> 26:13.950
Hey, what's the meaning of this?

26:14.160 --> 26:17.070
He's the real Hijikata-san...but
he's like a totally different person.

26:17.600 --> 26:19.570
Anyway... Hijikata-san...

26:19.730 --> 26:21.130
What is it, Mr. Shimura?

26:21.270 --> 26:23.850
Umm... What happened to work?

26:24.130 --> 26:26.180
You're hanging around here
in the middle of the day.

26:26.350 --> 26:27.300
Work?

26:27.660 --> 26:30.800
Oh, the Shinsengumi fired me.

26:30.800 --> 26:34.790
What? You quit the Shinsengumi?!
Why?!

26:35.610 --> 26:39.450
Well, I started to hate trifling
human relations.

26:39.450 --> 26:40.900
The job was dangerous, too.

26:41.250 --> 26:43.830
Besides, I'm not suited for it.

26:43.830 --> 26:46.900
I originally wanted to become
an anime voice actor.

26:46.900 --> 26:48.820
Really?! Is that true?!

26:48.820 --> 26:53.730
Well, I guess, right now, I'm looking
for a way to get by without working.

26:53.730 --> 26:55.580
I think working is for losers.

26:55.770 --> 26:58.180
He's a NEET!! He's thinking
like a NEET!!

26:58.180 --> 27:01.600
Oh yeah! Come to think of
it, you're like NEETs, too!

27:01.600 --> 27:04.000
Who are you calling a NEET?
Don't group us with them.

27:04.000 --> 27:07.050
How about it? Do you want
to form a group with me?

27:07.300 --> 27:10.770
Right now, I'm writing a
To Love-Ru dojinshi.

27:10.770 --> 27:13.060
Mr. Sakata, you know a
lot about JUMP, right?

27:13.570 --> 27:16.200
Want to make some money
at the Summer Comiket?

27:13.570 --> 27:16.200
[Note: Summer Comiket is a Convention
for dojinshi (amateur comics).]

27:16.200 --> 27:18.930
This won't sell!! This looks
like a kid drew it!!

27:19.150 --> 27:22.700
I'm stumped. I used up most
of my savings on a figurine.

27:23.100 --> 27:25.120
I guess I have to sell my sword.

27:25.120 --> 27:30.180
He's really pathetic! He's trying to sell
his samurai soul to get a figurine!!

27:30.180 --> 27:35.180
I've tried to sell it many times,
but I can't seem to let go of it.

27:36.160 --> 27:40.150
The guy at the store said that it was a cursed
demonic sword, but that can't be...

27:40.150 --> 27:42.800
Oh! Do you think that maybe I'll
wake up in the morning to find

27:42.800 --> 27:46.330
this demonic sword has changed into
a beautiful girl sleeping next to me?

27:46.330 --> 27:48.140
Oh! I'm beginning to love that idea...

27:48.960 --> 27:50.460
[Swordsmith]

27:50.770 --> 27:53.280
This blade pattern on the
front and the back...

27:53.480 --> 27:55.480
There's no mistake. This is Muramasha.

27:53.480 --> 27:55.480
[Note: Spoof of legendary evil sword "Muramasa."]

27:55.880 --> 27:56.880
Muramasha?

27:57.320 --> 28:01.500
It is a famous sword forged by Muramasha Senko,
a swordsmith from the Muromachi Era.

27:57.320 --> 28:01.500
[Note: Spoof of legendary swordsmith
"Senko Muramasa."]

28:02.340 --> 28:04.670
It is said to cut incredibly well.

28:04.670 --> 28:07.640
It is also known as a demonic sword
that devours human souls.

28:07.640 --> 28:10.350
A demonic sword? Is it really
a demonic sword?!

28:10.350 --> 28:12.850
Will a beautiful girl come out of it?!

28:12.850 --> 28:14.650
Well... Umm...

28:14.650 --> 28:15.830
A demonic sword?

28:16.320 --> 28:18.530
What kind of demonic sword is it?

28:19.060 --> 28:21.360
It apparently harbors the grudge
of a hikikomori boy

28:21.360 --> 28:24.010
who was slain by his mother
with the Muramasha.

28:24.010 --> 28:25.720
What kind of demonic sword is that?!

28:26.120 --> 28:28.630
According to legend, the son
never went to school...

28:28.810 --> 28:33.870
And always watched anime. But he said
he wanted to go on a school trip.

28:33.870 --> 28:35.850
As expected, his mother snapped.

28:36.490 --> 28:39.020
Muramasha is the sword she used.

28:39.020 --> 28:42.560
What a realistic legend! That
happened recently, didn't it?!

28:42.560 --> 28:44.680
That sounds like it was on
the news, doesn't it?!

28:44.680 --> 28:47.280
Those who carry Muramasha
at their sides

28:47.280 --> 28:49.900
will become possessed by the
grudge of the hikikomori son.

28:49.900 --> 28:54.100
Their interest in anime and two-dimensional
media will increase,

28:54.100 --> 28:59.290
and their interest in work and fighting
will decrease proportionately.

29:00.130 --> 29:02.660
In other words, he'll become
a hopeless otaku.

29:03.170 --> 29:05.480
But there are many counterfeits
of this sword.

29:05.480 --> 29:07.250
Even if it is a real sword,

29:07.250 --> 29:12.400
there's an even lower chance that
it's the sword of legend. But...

29:12.400 --> 29:16.960
If this is the real demon sword...

29:16.960 --> 29:21.150
There may not be anything left
of that man's original soul.

29:22.280 --> 29:26.900
It's likely the demonic sword has devoured him
and he's already become a different person.

29:27.960 --> 29:33.530
He'll probably never return
to his former self.

29:36.120 --> 29:39.380
Do you understand me, Shinohara-kun?

29:39.750 --> 29:42.840
What do you think is the greatest
misfortune for a warrior?

29:43.500 --> 29:45.720
It's the misfortune of not
being understood.

29:46.320 --> 29:48.690
No matter how much skill you have...

29:49.410 --> 29:54.510
No matter how hard you try, you
will never be judged properly.

29:55.100 --> 29:57.690
You will never be given food
that is suited for your stature.

29:57.690 --> 29:59.160
There is no greater misfortune.

29:59.880 --> 30:03.730
Like Li Mu of Zhao and Yue
Fei of Southern Song...

30:04.290 --> 30:07.290
There were many great generals who
faded away along with their skills...

30:07.290 --> 30:09.680
While serving stupid rulers.

30:10.340 --> 30:12.840
I also never had someone
who truly understood me.

30:13.730 --> 30:16.910
Even when I was called a
child prodigy at school,

30:16.910 --> 30:21.050
or when I mastered the distinguished Hokuto Itto,

30:21.770 --> 30:25.700
I went along with the times and even associated
with Anti-Foreigner Faction members.

30:25.700 --> 30:29.850
But wherever I went, nothing
was satisfying enough.

30:30.830 --> 30:34.640
I never thought that I
would find it here.

30:35.740 --> 30:38.760
That man understands me the most.

30:39.800 --> 30:44.920
That man knows I'm too good
for the Shinsengumi.

30:45.940 --> 30:49.280
He knows that I will not end
up serving the likes of Kondo.

30:49.620 --> 30:51.620
He knows what I thirst for...

30:56.870 --> 31:02.820
My greatest misfortune is that the person who
understands me the most is my enemy.

31:03.520 --> 31:04.830
Well, that's fine.

31:04.830 --> 31:08.630
If there isn't anyone who understands me,
I just have to make everyone recognize me.

31:08.630 --> 31:10.960
The most dangerous man is gone.

31:11.580 --> 31:12.630
All that's left

31:12.630 --> 31:17.640
is to kill Isao Kondo and make
the Shinsengumi mine.

31:19.140 --> 31:22.160
That man... It's as the Vice-Chief said...

31:22.690 --> 31:26.290
I need to tell the Vice-Chief... I need to
let the Vice-Chief know immediately.

31:30.350 --> 31:32.150
You... Could it be?!

31:32.970 --> 31:36.020
My, my, I came to smoke
my last cigarette.

31:36.020 --> 31:37.840
Of all the people to last see...

31:37.840 --> 31:40.020
I've become a total degenerate.

31:40.020 --> 31:47.710
Oh well... This is it for me... I'll cling
onto anything, even straw...

31:40.020 --> 31:47.710
[Note: From the proverb, "A drowning
man will grasp at a straw."]

31:48.170 --> 31:51.670
Listen up. This is my first
and last request for you.

31:54.630 --> 31:55.850
I never expected...

31:55.850 --> 31:59.650
Ito to be allied with them.

31:59.650 --> 32:01.420
I need to tell the Vice-Chief
immediately...

32:01.420 --> 32:02.420
The Vice-Chief ...

32:05.460 --> 32:06.860
Please...

32:06.860 --> 32:08.370
The Shinsengumi...

32:08.800 --> 32:11.840
My... Our Shinsengumi...

32:13.270 --> 32:14.770
Protect it...

32:16.630 --> 32:17.910
Please...

32:20.680 --> 32:22.610
Y-You're...

32:22.610 --> 32:25.020
The Kiheitai... Swordsman...

32:25.020 --> 32:26.960
Kawakami...
Bansai...

32:36.000 --> 32:37.650
I-Ito...

32:38.880 --> 32:40.580
You bastard...

32:40.580 --> 32:42.870
You were secretly associating
with the enemy.

32:42.870 --> 32:47.750
Yamazaki-kun, the world won't change
if we keep on sword fighting like you.

32:48.550 --> 32:50.750
We must be smarter.

32:51.050 --> 32:54.640
No matter how much we swing our swords,
we cannot stamp out crime.

32:55.190 --> 32:57.890
Furthermore, you mustn't forget
that if they weren't around,

32:57.890 --> 33:01.760
there would be no use for us police.

33:02.390 --> 33:06.000
I'm sure it would be better for
us to work with each other.

33:06.440 --> 33:10.950
We can become partners who work for each
other's profit and maintain balance.

33:11.350 --> 33:13.210
The Shinsengumi won't become
any stronger if we

33:13.210 --> 33:15.840
continue to do things the
way your superior does.

33:15.840 --> 33:18.790
I will change the Shinsengumi.

33:19.280 --> 33:21.900
It'll become stronger and bigger.

33:21.900 --> 33:26.410
And I, Kamotaro Ito, will become the
spear that shows our potential

33:26.410 --> 33:27.940
to take control of the country.

33:32.240 --> 33:33.820
Do what you want...

33:34.610 --> 33:37.370
But let me say this.

33:37.370 --> 33:43.060
We may be uneducated and can't
tell how skilled you are...

33:43.470 --> 33:49.770
But no one will follow an empty vessel
with no bushido or principles.

33:50.280 --> 33:53.710
I'll follow them...

33:54.280 --> 33:56.280
Until the end...

33:58.320 --> 34:02.120
You'll continue on struggling to inform them
of what you've discovered until the very end.

34:02.120 --> 34:05.090
As their spy, are you saying
that is part of your bushido?

34:06.350 --> 34:09.230
Bansai-dono, I leave the rest to you.

34:10.600 --> 34:14.900
I'll give you the honor of dying in a battle
against an Anti-Foreigner Faction member.

34:15.600 --> 34:20.360
Aren't you glad? You can maintain
that bushido you love so much.

34:20.360 --> 34:22.960
I'll be sure to tell that to your superiors.

34:22.960 --> 34:23.530
No...

34:23.530 --> 34:24.850
I suppose there's no need for that.

34:25.300 --> 34:28.780
They'll be headed to where
you're going soon enough.

34:36.630 --> 34:39.740
There's something going on within
the Shinsengumi right now.

34:39.740 --> 34:40.840
Is that it?

34:41.690 --> 34:45.110
Do you think Hijikata-san was fired from
the Shinsengumi because of that?

34:45.600 --> 34:49.830
Who knows? Well, whatever happens,
it's none of our business.

34:50.080 --> 34:52.100
Let's avoid getting involved any further.

34:52.100 --> 34:56.820
But Hijikata-san asked us
of all people to help him.

34:57.310 --> 34:59.350
Hijikata is very prideful.

34:59.350 --> 35:01.080
For him to put aside his
shame and self-respect,

35:01.080 --> 35:03.420
and ask someone to do something for
him... It must be pretty serious...

35:04.860 --> 35:06.320
Umm...

35:06.320 --> 35:08.310
Excuse me, Mr. Sakata, but...

35:08.790 --> 35:13.920
A rare limited-edition figurine
is going on sale tomorrow.

35:13.920 --> 35:16.700
It's limited to one per customer.

35:16.700 --> 35:24.150
But I want to buy three: one to preserve,
one to look at, and one to use.

35:24.400 --> 35:27.480
So I order you to come with me...

35:27.480 --> 35:30.430
You should get some shame
and self-respect!

35:30.430 --> 35:32.640
"To use"? What are you
planning to use it for?!

35:32.640 --> 35:35.500
I feel stupid for worrying about you!!

35:37.430 --> 35:38.370
[Shinsengumi]

35:38.590 --> 35:39.580
Vice-Chief ...

35:39.580 --> 35:40.610
We finally found you.

35:41.370 --> 35:43.180
Bad news, Vice-Chief!

35:43.180 --> 35:45.040
Come back to the squad immediately.

35:46.120 --> 35:47.790
What happened?

35:47.790 --> 35:50.110
Yamazaki-san... Yamazaki-san...

35:50.550 --> 35:52.780
Someone killed him.

35:54.360 --> 35:56.230
Y-Yamazaki-san?!

35:56.230 --> 36:00.620
We found him on the ground, covered
in blood just outside the headquarters.

36:00.620 --> 36:02.430
By that time...

36:02.830 --> 36:05.130
We still haven't found the killer.

36:05.130 --> 36:06.270
Anyway...

36:06.270 --> 36:08.000
Come back with us to the headquarters.

36:08.000 --> 36:08.850
Huh?

36:08.850 --> 36:11.180
But I was fired...

36:11.180 --> 36:13.370
Now's not the time to be saying that.

36:13.370 --> 36:14.370
Come on, quickly...

36:14.370 --> 36:15.370
Vice-Chief...

36:15.370 --> 36:16.840
Come join Yamazaki...

36:23.930 --> 36:25.390
Damn! They got away!

36:25.390 --> 36:26.340
After them!!

36:26.340 --> 36:28.450
Ow,ow,ow,ow,ow,ow. Mr. Sakata,

36:28.450 --> 36:31.030
the shoulder portion of my denim
jacket is grinding into me!!

36:31.030 --> 36:34.570
My arms feel like they're going to
rip off just like Guts from Berserk!!

36:31.030 --> 36:36.810
[Note: Guts is the main character of Berserk,
a popular manga from Hakusensha.]

36:34.570 --> 36:36.810
Shut up!! You be quiet!!

36:38.110 --> 36:39.640
What was the meaning of that?!

36:39.640 --> 36:41.740
Why is the Shinsengumi after Hijikata?!

36:42.550 --> 36:43.980
Mr. Sakata!

36:55.010 --> 36:57.670
Whoa, Miss Kagura. That was amazing!

36:57.670 --> 37:00.150
This is like the return of Miss
Arale from Dr. Slump...

36:57.670 --> 37:03.110
[Note: Dr. Slump is a manga by Akira
Toriyama, author of Dragon Ball.]

37:00.150 --> 37:03.110
Shut up!! Someone shut this guy up!!

37:15.760 --> 37:20.120
This is Third Squad. This is Third
Squad. Come in. Over.

37:20.750 --> 37:22.080
Did you find Hijikata?

37:23.260 --> 37:28.710
We found him, but we were no match
for his incredibly cute and strong ally.

37:28.710 --> 37:29.750
Over, uh-huh.

37:29.750 --> 37:30.570
"Uh-huh"?

37:31.570 --> 37:33.680
Do whatever it takes to kill him.

37:33.680 --> 37:37.230
Even if we kill Kondo, it'll be
meaningless if Hijikata's still around.

37:37.230 --> 37:40.630
Get rid of all the dangerous elements
before we assassinate Kondo.

37:40.630 --> 37:42.800
Once Kondo and Hijikata are both gone,

37:42.800 --> 37:46.890
the entire Shinsengumi will become
faithful to the Ito faction.

37:47.060 --> 37:49.620
They're planning to assassinate
Kondo-san and Hijikata-san?!

37:49.890 --> 37:52.890
Don't let any other squad members
aside from us find out.

37:52.890 --> 37:56.190
Make it look as if Anti-Foreigner
Faction members did it.

37:56.190 --> 38:01.130
If Ito-san's plan is exposed at this stage,
the Shinsengumi will be split in two.

38:01.880 --> 38:04.900
Kondo's assassination
looks to be a success.

38:04.900 --> 38:06.750
Right now, he's on a train
heading to an expedition

38:06.750 --> 38:09.920
to recruit squad members,
just as Ito-san planned.

38:10.350 --> 38:13.600
All of the squad members
with him are allied with us.

38:16.070 --> 38:18.330
He's by himself...

38:18.330 --> 38:20.080
Kondo is

38:20.360 --> 38:21.920
going to hell.

38:23.220 --> 38:25.760
It's been a while since I've
gone back to Bushu.

38:23.220 --> 38:29.490
[Note: Also known as Musashi Province. Today, it
comprises of Tokyo, Saitama and part of Kanagawa.]

38:26.280 --> 38:29.490
That's where Toshi, Sougo and I grew up.

38:29.490 --> 38:32.830
It was a rough place where
there were always fights.

38:33.300 --> 38:36.790
Come to think of it, it's no different
from what we're doing now.

38:37.520 --> 38:39.450
Sometimes I get anxious.

38:39.450 --> 38:42.620
I could have been a better
guy back then.

38:42.620 --> 38:44.710
I could have advanced a little.

38:46.140 --> 38:48.190
You're a wonderful samurai.

38:48.610 --> 38:52.040
I've never met a person
more honest than you.

38:52.040 --> 38:54.260
I suppose I could call you immaculate.

38:54.260 --> 38:56.550
You're like a white cloth.

38:56.950 --> 39:00.020
You accept anything and
are colored by all colors.

39:00.020 --> 39:01.950
The Shinsengumi

39:01.950 --> 39:06.730
is a flag made of a white cloth onto which
everyone may project his colors.

39:07.710 --> 39:09.640
In comparison, my color is black.

39:10.280 --> 39:14.050
I'm not colored by anything,
and I turn everything black.

39:14.680 --> 39:16.830
Only black remains, no matter where I go.

39:17.260 --> 39:21.060
Everywhere I go becomes my color.

39:24.500 --> 39:27.140
Kondo-san, I'm sorry.

39:28.010 --> 39:31.830
Your flag has become pitch black.

39:36.950 --> 39:38.650
As expected, Sensei.

39:38.870 --> 39:40.900
You say interesting things.

39:40.900 --> 39:43.270
We've become pitch black?

39:43.660 --> 39:48.160
I see. That would be true
if I were a white cloth.

39:48.850 --> 39:50.270
But I'm...

39:50.270 --> 39:55.400
a loincloth that's full of frizzy hair. A white flag?

39:56.840 --> 39:58.910
I'm not that naïve.

39:59.520 --> 40:02.920
I don't know about those around
you, but they're different.

40:03.620 --> 40:07.010
They can't be called a color.

40:07.650 --> 40:09.880
If anything, they're grime.

40:10.490 --> 40:13.660
They're stains that you can't remove,
no matter how much you wash.

40:13.660 --> 40:16.580
They're persistent and can't
be removed by washing.

40:16.580 --> 40:20.670
I ended up becoming attached
to them. It's a real bother.

40:21.680 --> 40:27.560
But the stains began to gather, and as
time passed, they became visible.

40:28.070 --> 40:31.090
Before I knew it, they'd become
a splendid flag.

40:31.970 --> 40:34.200
They're uneducated and have no ideals.

40:34.680 --> 40:37.310
They act according to emotion
more than logic.

40:38.480 --> 40:40.480
I don't often know what they're thinking.

40:40.480 --> 40:42.140
They're mysterious guys.

40:42.540 --> 40:43.910
Sensei, you...

40:43.910 --> 40:45.560
can't control them.

40:46.960 --> 40:50.740
They can't be colored or
affected by anything.

40:53.200 --> 40:55.340
Okita-kun, what are you doing?

40:55.340 --> 40:56.910
You're supposed to be keeping watch.

40:56.910 --> 40:58.780
What are you doing?

40:59.920 --> 41:04.210
I'm asking you what you're
doing, you piece of shit.

41:04.210 --> 41:05.600
Okita-kun...

41:05.600 --> 41:07.250
How dare you talk like that to Ito Sensei?!

41:07.780 --> 41:08.810
Let go.

41:14.620 --> 41:18.050
I said, let go of him!!

41:28.450 --> 41:30.060
Sougo...

41:31.480 --> 41:35.520
Okita-kun, so you really were
part of Hijikata's faction.

41:38.430 --> 41:42.480
You were a spy who got close to me
to find out what I was going to do.

41:43.030 --> 41:47.550
Your betrayal of Hijikata was
all an act to fool me.

41:48.420 --> 41:49.500
That wasn't an act.

41:50.500 --> 41:58.080
I told you... All I want is to be Vice-Chief.
I'll crush anyone who gets in my way.

41:59.370 --> 42:05.280
Hijikata disappeared... You're next, Ito Sensei.

42:06.700 --> 42:13.000
I don't want to work under him
or you. I have only one boss.

42:14.410 --> 42:18.110
Out of the way! That spot
by his side is mine!!

42:20.380 --> 42:25.560
How ill-natured. You used
me to get rid of Hijikata.

42:25.560 --> 42:28.260
And, now that I'm of no use,
you're going to get rid of me.

42:28.260 --> 42:32.640
Why not? I have the same idea as you.

42:51.200 --> 42:55.910
Kondo-san!! At this rate, Kondo-san
will be assassinated!!

42:56.170 --> 42:58.380
It's none of my concern...
It's none of my concern...

42:58.480 --> 43:00.050
It's none of my concern...

43:00.050 --> 43:03.390
Hijikata-san!! Get a hold
of yourself, Hijikata-san!!

43:03.390 --> 43:05.890
It's none of my concern...
It's of no concern...

43:05.890 --> 43:08.790
At this rate, you may lose all
the people and things...

43:08.790 --> 43:11.940
You hold dear!!

43:13.230 --> 43:16.160
It's of no concern... It's
none of my concern...

43:17.870 --> 43:20.370
Gin-chan, what should we do?

43:22.730 --> 43:24.510
Please protect...

43:24.510 --> 43:27.470
Our Shinsengumi...

43:27.970 --> 43:32.180
Kagura, patch us through to
headquarters and all cars.

43:32.180 --> 43:33.380
Aye, aye, sir.

43:38.910 --> 43:42.650
Umm... Hello? Can you hear
me you tax thieves?

43:42.650 --> 43:45.400
I'm not sure if it's the Ito faction
or the Mayonnaise faction...

43:45.790 --> 43:48.420
But I'm saying this to
all of you tax thieves!

43:48.420 --> 43:51.730
Immediately leave your posts and
go after the train that Kondo's on.

43:51.890 --> 43:54.230
If you waste time, your boss...

43:54.230 --> 43:55.750
Might be killed.

43:55.730 --> 43:58.870
This is an order. Those
who ignore this order...

43:58.870 --> 44:01.800
Will have to commit seppuku for
not standing by their bushido.

44:01.800 --> 44:03.970
Is this a prank?! Who are you?!

44:03.970 --> 44:08.060
Who do you think you're
talking to? Who am I?

44:08.660 --> 44:13.200
This is Shinsengumi Vice-Chief
Toshiro Hijikata, damn it!!

44:13.720 --> 44:14.930
Humph!

44:14.930 --> 44:16.170
Gin-san...

44:16.470 --> 44:18.420
I'm sick of seeing that cowardly face.

44:18.630 --> 44:20.000
This is convenient.

44:20.000 --> 44:23.070
If the Shinsengumi is going to disappear,
you can disappear with them.

44:23.800 --> 44:25.630
I'll send you to your grave.

44:25.630 --> 44:28.630
No way! I'm not going!

44:28.630 --> 44:30.530
I wasn't talking to you!!

44:32.850 --> 44:35.580
Hey, are you listening? Are you?

44:35.720 --> 44:37.600
Don't retreat and shove your
problems onto other people!!

44:37.600 --> 44:40.380
Are you the type that asks
things of others?

44:40.620 --> 44:43.540
Are you the type that

44:43.540 --> 44:47.400
shoves the fate of your Shinsengumi
onto someone else?

44:47.980 --> 44:49.170
If you're going to die,

44:49.170 --> 44:52.720
die while swinging your sword along side
the things that are important to you!!

44:52.720 --> 44:54.330
That's who you are!!

44:59.590 --> 45:00.990
That hurts...

45:00.990 --> 45:02.790
I told you, that hurts!!

45:07.720 --> 45:09.170
Could it be?

45:09.430 --> 45:10.990
Could it be?!

45:13.360 --> 45:17.510
Ito Sensei, the train is on fire! It's
dangerous for us to stay here!

45:18.300 --> 45:21.840
Don't stop the train!! If we
stop, Kondo will escape.

45:21.840 --> 45:25.300
Everyone on this train aside from
those two are our allies.

45:25.300 --> 45:29.000
As long as this train continues
moving, they're trapped like rats.

45:30.610 --> 45:37.070
Sorry, Sougo. It's all my
fault this happened.

45:37.740 --> 45:41.730
How can I make it up
to you? How can I...

45:41.730 --> 45:47.120
apologize to you...to Toshi?
How can I apologize?

45:48.950 --> 45:50.280
Sougo!!

45:50.670 --> 45:54.420
What are you doing, Sougo?! Open up!!

45:54.420 --> 45:56.050
Kondo-san...

45:56.720 --> 45:59.680
If our boss is killed, we'll lose this battle.

46:00.380 --> 46:02.310
Please stay here.

46:02.310 --> 46:03.290
No way!!

46:06.010 --> 46:10.000
Kondo-san, I've constantly told you

46:10.000 --> 46:13.400
that the bad thing about you is
that you're too good a person.

46:13.870 --> 46:16.880
You believe anyone and
never doubt them.

46:19.440 --> 46:23.630
In the end, a fox like him
ended up by your side.

46:26.170 --> 46:30.180
Well, I expected this would
happen sooner or later.

46:31.320 --> 46:36.190
But because you're like that,
we gathered around you...

46:36.530 --> 46:40.640
Because you're like that,
we fought with you.

46:41.410 --> 46:43.280
Because you're like that...

46:43.830 --> 46:46.520
You're worth risking my life to protect.

46:47.390 --> 46:50.520
Sougo! Wait!!

46:52.110 --> 46:56.030
If you die, I... I...

46:57.760 --> 47:01.050
Sougo!!

47:10.340 --> 47:15.490
Okita-kun, I thought you
were smarter than that.

47:15.880 --> 47:19.220
Do you plan to fight us all by yourself?

47:20.620 --> 47:24.800
You let Kondo escape and remained
behind with the enemy.

47:24.800 --> 47:27.380
Do you plan to die a heroic death?

47:28.030 --> 47:35.270
Unfortunately, Kondo is going
to die according to my plans.

47:35.850 --> 47:39.120
We aren't the only ones
on this battlefield.

47:42.260 --> 47:44.190
The Kiheitai, huh?

47:49.600 --> 47:53.910
Sorry, Ito-san. Actually,
I'm not alone either.

48:00.940 --> 48:03.350
Impossible... That's...

48:05.860 --> 48:09.090
This is a raid!!

48:09.090 --> 48:12.160
All of you surrender quietly!!

48:12.650 --> 48:14.160
Hijikata?!

48:14.900 --> 48:17.040
Why is he here?!

48:19.370 --> 48:22.640
Can't you act cool for just a little longer?!

48:22.640 --> 48:25.150
I can't, I can't! It's impossible
for me! I'm scared!!

48:25.150 --> 48:27.280
In order to raise the morale of your allies,

48:27.280 --> 48:30.840
you need to show them that their
Vice-Chief is still kicking!!

48:31.590 --> 48:37.440
You've got to be kidding me! You only
reverted back when you hit me?!

48:37.440 --> 48:40.300
Tsk... A bunch of eyesores
have crawled out...

48:41.550 --> 48:46.870
But an army isn't enough
to take them down.

48:48.940 --> 48:50.670
Hijikata...

48:53.720 --> 48:59.620
What can he do by showing up now?
I'll wipe them all out, including Kondo.

49:01.080 --> 49:03.020
You're the ones who are
going to get wiped out.

49:04.320 --> 49:06.460
I see some faces I know.

49:06.790 --> 49:13.410
I hope you're prepared to
die for joining that side.

49:14.330 --> 49:17.610
Shinsengumi Regulation Article 21...

49:17.810 --> 49:22.000
Those who have been secretly conspiring
with the enemy shall be punished!

49:27.990 --> 49:32.750
I'll take down all of you.

49:36.380 --> 49:39.260
Don't you see the situation you're in?

49:39.830 --> 49:42.980
Here, I'm the faction in power.

49:43.380 --> 49:46.590
You're the rebel.

49:47.080 --> 49:51.160
The laws that he created have
no meaning anymore.

49:51.470 --> 49:54.290
Your Shinsengumi will disappear.

50:01.310 --> 50:02.800
Get rid of him.

50:02.800 --> 50:03.950
Yes!

50:07.080 --> 50:09.890
As the First Squad Captain
of the Shinsengumi,

50:10.180 --> 50:13.450
I shall give you your final lesson.

50:13.920 --> 50:17.950
When faced with an enemy who
is considerably more powerful,

50:17.950 --> 50:21.240
it is best to overcome that power
with sheer numbers.

50:21.810 --> 50:23.830
Synchronize your breathing.

50:25.480 --> 50:27.670
Build up spirit in your heart and body.

50:27.850 --> 50:30.580
When you are at your peak...

50:31.840 --> 50:34.080
Attack all at once!!

50:37.170 --> 50:38.950
And...!!

50:50.270 --> 50:52.470
Die.

50:57.300 --> 50:59.710
Are those Anti-Foreigner
Faction members?

51:00.660 --> 51:05.250
Jeez... It looks like it wasn't
just an internal squabble.

51:06.810 --> 51:08.670
Kondo-san...

51:08.670 --> 51:11.090
Where in the world is Kondo-san?!

51:11.090 --> 51:12.130
There!

51:12.130 --> 51:14.390
That car that's moving
far behind the train!

51:14.390 --> 51:17.030
All the enemies are headed there!

51:20.070 --> 51:24.270
That's the situation, Mr. Hijikata.
Take care of the rest yourself!!

51:25.880 --> 51:28.310
Hey, wait, Mr. Sakata!

51:28.350 --> 51:31.660
Are you planning to leave me here?!

51:31.660 --> 51:35.150
That's as reckless as sending Mr. Yamcha
to Planet Namek by himself.

51:31.660 --> 51:35.150
[Note: Parody of Dragon Ball. Yamcha
is thought of as the weakest character.]

51:35.150 --> 51:38.600
And leaving him to decide
the fate of the universe!!

51:38.600 --> 51:42.270
It's all right! You're Vegeta!!
You can do it if you try!

51:38.600 --> 51:42.270
[Note: Parody of Dragon Ball. Vegeta
is one of the strong characters.]

51:42.270 --> 51:43.300
Mr. Sakata!!

51:45.300 --> 51:47.130
Vice-Chief!!

51:47.370 --> 51:49.000
It's the Vice-Chief!

51:49.000 --> 51:50.870
The Vice-Chief is all right!!

51:50.870 --> 51:53.700
No matter how you look
at this, I'm not all right!!

51:53.700 --> 51:55.860
So you've finally come.

51:56.050 --> 52:00.610
I was getting sick of taking care
of him. Take him already.

52:00.880 --> 52:03.580
He's caused us a lot of trouble.

52:03.580 --> 52:05.650
Have the shogunate transfer the
reward into my bank account.

52:05.650 --> 52:08.960
Ito, that bastard, has finally
shown his true self!!

52:08.960 --> 52:13.450
But we're all right now that
the Vice-Chief is back!!

52:08.960 --> 52:13.450
Hey, are you listening? Transfer my
reward into my bank account...

52:13.910 --> 52:20.400
Vice-Chief, we shall confront the enemy.
You save the Chief in the meantime.

52:20.640 --> 52:21.560
Let's go!!

52:21.560 --> 52:22.980
Hey, wait!!

52:23.160 --> 52:25.300
Hey, wait, damn it!

52:25.300 --> 52:28.400
Something weird has happened
to your Vice-Chief.

52:28.400 --> 52:29.340
Listen to me, baldy!!

52:44.830 --> 52:46.890
Those guys... Why?

52:48.760 --> 52:49.980
Why?!

53:01.010 --> 53:04.740
You idiot... Why are you...

53:05.230 --> 53:09.060
Why are you here?

53:09.090 --> 53:12.120
I treated you so badly.

53:12.350 --> 53:15.190
Why did you come all this way for me?

53:17.710 --> 53:20.100
Toshi!

53:21.410 --> 53:23.550
Why did you come?

53:25.320 --> 53:27.670
You idiot!

53:27.670 --> 53:28.340
Huh?

53:32.950 --> 53:35.640
Kondo-san, are you all right?

53:37.310 --> 53:39.480
It's no good. He's not here.

53:39.480 --> 53:41.940
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

53:41.940 --> 53:44.490
Oh, there he is! Are you all right?

53:44.630 --> 53:49.150
Hey, it seems that people are really
trying to assassinate you.

53:49.150 --> 53:52.160
No, I was almost killed by you just now!!

53:55.360 --> 53:59.170
Could it be that you dragged
Toshi all the way here?

54:02.050 --> 54:05.410
This is impossible. You help us?

54:08.570 --> 54:11.580
It was his last request.

54:11.580 --> 54:12.880
His last request?

54:12.880 --> 54:15.540
His soul was devoured
by a demonic sword.

54:15.840 --> 54:19.050
Right now, he's just a hopeless otaku.

54:19.050 --> 54:20.900
He won't return ever again.

54:21.680 --> 54:23.430
A demonic sword?

54:25.000 --> 54:28.570
While in that state, what
did Toshi ask you to do?

54:28.800 --> 54:32.510
He asked us to protect the Shinsengumi.

54:35.680 --> 54:39.580
It would be a pain to do that, so I brought
him here and told him to do it himself.

54:39.950 --> 54:44.670
Our job ends here. I want you
to transfer the reward to me.

54:48.000 --> 54:53.310
I will... I'll give you all of my savings...

54:53.710 --> 54:57.250
But, Odd Jobs, I have a request for you.

54:59.310 --> 55:01.800
Consider this a last request as well.

55:02.740 --> 55:05.770
Take Toshi and run away.

55:06.310 --> 55:09.030
It's my fault this happened.

55:09.820 --> 55:13.150
I don't want Toshi to get involved
in this battle in his current state.

55:13.470 --> 55:18.240
I ignored Toshi's advice to be wary of Ito.

55:18.520 --> 55:24.750
Furthermore, I punished Toshi for
a petty blunder on Ito's advice.

55:24.930 --> 55:28.050
I never even knew that this
was happening to him.

55:28.580 --> 55:33.800
I didn't know that he was trying to protect
the Shinsengumi, even in his condition.

55:34.340 --> 55:39.050
I didn't know that, despite his
pride, he lowered his head...

55:39.050 --> 55:41.360
And entrusted the Shinsengumi to you.

55:44.050 --> 55:49.610
I'm sorry, Toshi... I'm sorry, everyone...

55:51.420 --> 55:57.080
I...I'm...a big idiot...

55:58.710 --> 56:03.380
Tell all the cars to immediately
leave the battlefront.

56:04.110 --> 56:06.210
Isao Kondo has died in battle.

56:06.820 --> 56:10.720
I don't want my friends to fight
each other any more.

56:15.620 --> 56:21.480
Gentlemen of the Yamato,
our Chief, Isao Kondo...

56:15.620 --> 56:21.480
[Note: Spoof of the Space Battleship Yamato anime series.]

56:21.480 --> 56:23.120
has been safely rescued.

56:23.560 --> 56:25.830
Victory is within our grasp!

56:26.250 --> 56:28.460
We shall get revenge on

56:28.460 --> 56:32.540
that lawless bunch for besmirching
our Chief's name. Let me say this.

56:28.460 --> 56:32.540
[Note: Spoof of GUNDAM series anime.]

56:32.540 --> 56:34.410
They are all scum!

56:34.410 --> 56:37.190
In the name of the moon...

56:34.410 --> 56:38.770
[Spoof of Sailor Moon.]

56:37.190 --> 56:38.770
We will punish them!!

56:38.770 --> 56:41.570
Hey, who's that? Who's making that silly speech?

56:42.010 --> 56:46.010
Who am I? I'm Shinsengumi Vice-Chief...

56:46.010 --> 56:49.150
Toshiro Hijikata nari!!

56:46.010 --> 56:49.150
[Note: Suffix "Nari" was used by Samurai and by
Korosuke in the Kiteretsu Daihyakka anime.]

56:51.850 --> 56:53.540
HIjikata-san...

56:53.990 --> 56:58.180
Mr. Kondo, we shall protect your life.

56:58.180 --> 57:02.000
In return, you have an obligation to fulfill.

57:02.640 --> 57:04.520
To not die.

57:05.080 --> 57:06.810
Do whatever it takes to live.

57:06.810 --> 57:09.120
No matter how humiliating it may be...

57:09.120 --> 57:14.290
No matter how many squad members
die before your eyes, you must live!

57:14.580 --> 57:16.540
As long as you're here,

57:16.540 --> 57:18.350
the Shinsengumi is not finished.

57:18.850 --> 57:22.690
We joined the Shinsengumi because
we wanted to be with you...

57:23.880 --> 57:24.990
You're an idiot.

57:24.990 --> 57:27.120
Don't think about such difficult things!

57:27.890 --> 57:31.140
You should live the way you want to live.

57:32.830 --> 57:36.820
We just have to protect
you from everyone.

57:37.000 --> 57:38.650
Kondo-san...

57:42.770 --> 57:45.820
You are the soul of the Shinsengumi.

57:45.820 --> 57:48.090
We are the sword that protects you.

57:48.600 --> 57:50.230
Toshi...

57:51.420 --> 57:54.600
You broke once before.
What can you protect?

57:55.750 --> 58:01.220
Hijikata-kun, it seems we have
to settle things between us.

58:01.220 --> 58:04.920
I have a sword right here.
One that cuts very well.

58:09.670 --> 58:13.660
Odd Jobs, I heard your rotten sermon!

58:13.660 --> 58:14.910
What is it?

58:14.910 --> 58:17.400
Don't talk as if you're so high and mighty.

58:21.170 --> 58:23.360
Draw it already!

58:23.360 --> 58:24.540
Shut up!

58:26.910 --> 58:29.540
I have one more thing to say to you.

58:33.010 --> 58:35.280
Thank you!!

58:35.650 --> 58:39.770
Hey, hey, it looks like the demonic
sword devoured him again...

58:39.770 --> 58:41.900
Toshi? Is that Toshi?

58:42.790 --> 58:44.840
I'm...

58:44.840 --> 58:50.370
Shinsengumi Vice-Chief
Toshiro Hijikata!!

58:50.970 --> 58:54.010
He fought off the demonic
sword's curse by himself.

58:54.010 --> 58:55.840
Sorry, Gorilla.

58:55.840 --> 58:59.870
Unfortunately, we can't take your request
no matter how much money you offer us.

59:00.100 --> 59:01.950
He was our client first.

59:02.230 --> 59:04.860
Didn't your job end already?

59:04.860 --> 59:07.300
I'm going to be charging overtime pay!

59:10.490 --> 59:12.750
Come on, Ito!

59:13.280 --> 59:18.190
It changed... The rhythm of that
man's soul has changed.

59:18.190 --> 59:22.660
It went from a childish anime song
to a sturdy rock-and-roll tune.

59:22.660 --> 59:26.200
I guess the same goes
for you, too, Ito-dono.

59:26.830 --> 59:31.210
You've gone from very dignified classical
music to fierce heavy metal.

59:31.790 --> 59:37.680
That's a nice song... Play your beautiful
concerto to your heart's content.

59:38.450 --> 59:40.480
Hijikata!!

59:40.480 --> 59:43.150
Ito!!

59:51.530 --> 59:53.500
The steering wheel...!

59:53.500 --> 59:54.640
Hey, behind us!!

59:59.450 --> 01:00:02.860
Kondo-san, move over
to this side already.

01:00:03.490 --> 01:00:08.420
I overworked myself a bit... I'm
getting overtime pay for this, right?

01:00:08.420 --> 01:00:09.420
Sougo?!

01:00:10.580 --> 01:00:15.230
I'll make sure you negotiate with
the person in charge of our pay.

01:00:15.230 --> 01:00:19.760
That's good. Also, make
sure to take care of him.

01:00:20.260 --> 01:00:23.290
I'm a little tired...

01:00:25.030 --> 01:00:30.900
Hijikata-san, if you come out even
a little behind, I'll kill you.

01:00:31.850 --> 01:00:35.910
The next time you show
weakness, I'll take...

01:00:36.590 --> 01:00:38.830
your position as Vice-Chief.

01:00:38.970 --> 01:00:42.920
But are you saying that I should
just leave Toshi and run away?

01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:44.920
Don't waste your time!!

01:00:44.920 --> 01:00:46.720
Don't fight here!!

01:00:46.720 --> 01:00:51.000
Why are you using me like
a bridge as if it's normal?!

01:00:54.160 --> 01:00:55.890
Gin-san!

01:01:07.980 --> 01:01:12.730
Hijikata-kun, you were the only
one who understood me.

01:01:13.450 --> 01:01:19.190
Unfortunately, you knew and feared my
potential and we became enemies.

01:01:19.470 --> 01:01:25.170
If you were Chief, I might have
never planned this rebellion.

01:01:26.330 --> 01:01:28.390
This is just hypothetical, though.

01:01:29.420 --> 01:01:33.820
But there's one thing you've
got wrong about me.

01:01:34.200 --> 01:01:40.580
Just as you know my potential,
I also know your potential.

01:01:41.300 --> 01:01:43.780
Toshiro Hijikata, bring it on!!

01:01:48.020 --> 01:01:50.850
This is the final showdown!!

01:02:06.950 --> 01:02:09.920
You have an interesting sound.

01:02:10.070 --> 01:02:15.760
Your sound is haphazard, willful,
and vague. It's akin to jazz.

01:02:16.080 --> 01:02:22.890
But it's undignified. If anything,
it's a drunk's humming.

01:02:22.890 --> 01:02:26.610
You bastard... You're the guy
who was with Takasugi.

01:02:28.610 --> 01:02:32.390
Hey, take your headphones off
when you talk to someone.

01:02:32.650 --> 01:02:37.190
Gintoki Sakata... No, Shiroyasha...

01:02:37.480 --> 01:02:41.790
Why are you with the Shinsengumi?

01:02:41.790 --> 01:02:44.110
You can hear me, can't you?

01:02:45.150 --> 01:02:49.620
That man seems to be
under your influence.

01:02:50.470 --> 01:02:55.610
Are you planning to spy on the Bakufu
once you take control of the Shinsengumi?

01:02:55.610 --> 01:03:02.620
We're not generous enough to be allied
with those who easily betray others.

01:03:02.950 --> 01:03:09.290
We also know that people will not gather
under a person who has been unfaithful.

01:03:09.420 --> 01:03:11.740
So what of that man?

01:03:12.300 --> 01:03:14.630
He is a pitiful man.

01:03:15.840 --> 01:03:19.870
By the time he realizes his
capacity, it'll be too late.

01:03:21.700 --> 01:03:24.590
It'll be after everything
breaks into pieces.

01:03:29.750 --> 01:03:32.210
Go to sleep, Ito...

01:03:32.760 --> 01:03:35.190
Along with the Shinsengumi...

01:03:50.840 --> 01:03:55.760
Geniuses are always alone. I have
no one who understands me.

01:03:56.350 --> 01:03:59.760
I shouldn't remain in a place like this.

01:04:00.070 --> 01:04:04.800
No one understands that. No
one realizes my true worth.

01:04:05.070 --> 01:04:05.920
In that case,

01:04:05.920 --> 01:04:08.800
I just have to demonstrate my potential
to take control of the country.

01:04:10.820 --> 01:04:13.370
I will take control of the Shinsengumi.

01:04:13.640 --> 01:04:16.830
I will use that as a foundation
to take control of the country.

01:04:17.100 --> 01:04:20.490
I, Kamotaro Ito, will take control of the
country as proof that I have lived.

01:04:21.170 --> 01:04:24.040
I will etch that into people's hearts.

01:04:24.040 --> 01:04:26.120
You don't mind acquiring
a bad reputation?

01:04:26.270 --> 01:04:28.140
In order to achieve what you propose,

01:04:28.140 --> 01:04:31.040
you have to wipe out Kondo,
whom you are indebted to.

01:04:31.040 --> 01:04:34.870
Indebted? Kondo's the one who
should be indebted to me.

01:04:35.310 --> 01:04:39.220
I'm working for an incompetent
man like him.

01:04:39.620 --> 01:04:43.050
He should be thankful. He has no
reason to be dissatisfied with me.

01:04:44.450 --> 01:04:46.310
Ito, you're the kind of person

01:04:46.420 --> 01:04:51.060
who thinks that everyone aside from
yourself is stupid, aren't you?

01:04:51.370 --> 01:04:56.740
But you're unsatisfied that those stupid
people don't understand you.

01:04:56.900 --> 01:05:02.070
You want them to understand you.
You want them to acknowledge you.

01:05:02.450 --> 01:05:08.070
You want to prove your worth?
It's not that difficult.

01:05:09.820 --> 01:05:13.080
You choose to be all by yourself.

01:05:13.400 --> 01:05:18.270
You don't want someone who
understands and accepts you.

01:05:18.390 --> 01:05:20.820
What you really want is...

01:05:28.910 --> 01:05:30.560
Where am I?

01:05:34.310 --> 01:05:36.140
Hijikata?

01:05:36.140 --> 01:05:40.790
I see... I won! I finally
won against Hijikata...

01:05:52.810 --> 01:05:56.430
Shinsuke saw through Ito.

01:05:56.620 --> 01:05:59.790
He is a show-off who has more
pride than anyone else

01:05:59.790 --> 01:06:03.340
and doesn't know his own worth.

01:06:03.340 --> 01:06:07.240
It was easy to provoke and use him.

01:06:07.560 --> 01:06:10.590
As expected, the Shinsengumi members
fought against each other

01:06:10.590 --> 01:06:12.850
and depleted their fighting potential.

01:06:12.850 --> 01:06:18.580
You were planning to use him to crush
the Shinsengumi to begin with.

01:06:18.690 --> 01:06:22.830
You acted as if you were helping
with Ito's rebellion.

01:06:22.830 --> 01:06:25.100
While you were really planning
to annihilate the Shinsengumi

01:06:25.100 --> 01:06:27.230
when it was exhausted after they
fought amongst themselves.

01:06:27.670 --> 01:06:30.700
It's a death that suits that
man, don't you think?

01:06:33.010 --> 01:06:36.590
The traitor is wiped out by the traitor.

01:06:37.390 --> 01:06:39.380
S-Stop!

01:06:40.470 --> 01:06:41.300
Stop!

01:06:44.630 --> 01:06:47.490
I'm not meant to die in a place like this.

01:06:48.160 --> 01:06:52.460
Stop. I can do much better...

01:06:52.460 --> 01:06:54.580
Much, much better...

01:06:56.430 --> 01:06:58.690
Mother!

01:06:58.690 --> 01:07:02.170
Take a look! I got a perfect
score on a test at school.

01:07:02.170 --> 01:07:06.340
Kamotaro, be quiet. It's bad for
your older brother's health.

01:07:08.010 --> 01:07:10.480
I-I'm very sorry.

01:07:11.060 --> 01:07:13.950
I've got to try much, much harder.

01:07:14.820 --> 01:07:19.220
If I try harder, I'm sure she'll notice me.

01:07:21.260 --> 01:07:23.930
Yes. That's wonderful, Kamotaro!

01:07:23.930 --> 01:07:27.110
You are the first child prodigy
to come from our school.

01:07:27.160 --> 01:07:29.980
Everyone, don't lose to Kamotaro.

01:07:32.370 --> 01:07:34.490
Don't get cocky.

01:07:34.490 --> 01:07:36.740
You're just a rich kid who
only knows how to study!

01:07:42.720 --> 01:07:45.750
I've got to try much, much harder.

01:07:45.970 --> 01:07:49.500
If I try harder, I'm sure that
everyone will accept me.

01:07:52.920 --> 01:07:56.460
One point! Wonderful. You're
really something, Kamo!

01:07:56.930 --> 01:07:59.000
Such an aptitude for swords at your age.

01:07:59.060 --> 01:08:00.800
You worked hard, didn't you?

01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:02.540
Kamo, go to Edo.

01:08:02.540 --> 01:08:06.050
I'll recommend you to the dojo of the
distinguished Hokuto Itto Style.

01:08:07.040 --> 01:08:10.550
Your brilliance will go to waste
out here in the country!

01:08:10.550 --> 01:08:15.010
It's possible you might even surpass the
great swordsman Musashi Miyamoto!

01:08:15.170 --> 01:08:16.880
Why?

01:08:16.930 --> 01:08:22.250
[Letter of Recommendation]

01:08:17.250 --> 01:08:22.250
Honestly. My heir, Takahisa is so sickly.

01:08:22.250 --> 01:08:24.760
I wonder what's going to
happen to the Ito family.

01:08:24.760 --> 01:08:27.760
Kamotaro grew up so healthily.

01:08:27.950 --> 01:08:32.470
No matter how brilliant our second
son is, it's just a waste of talent.

01:08:32.780 --> 01:08:37.100
Takahisa wasn't born to have everything
taken away from him by Kamotaro.

01:08:37.100 --> 01:08:43.270
I'm sure Kamotaro took everything away
from Takahisa while he was in my womb.

01:08:43.270 --> 01:08:46.280
I wish he was never born.

01:08:47.980 --> 01:08:52.630
Hey! What if Kamotaro hears you?!
What's the matter with you?!

01:08:52.630 --> 01:08:56.380
I feel so sorry for Takahisa.

01:08:56.380 --> 01:09:00.640
When I see Kamotaro carelessly
running about...

01:09:01.000 --> 01:09:03.620
You must be tired from taking
care of Takahisa.

01:09:03.620 --> 01:09:05.090
Go to bed already.

01:09:06.100 --> 01:09:10.420
Why? Why doesn't anyone look at me?

01:09:11.300 --> 01:09:15.560
I've tried so hard. I'm not at fault.

01:09:16.010 --> 01:09:19.970
Look at me. Praise me.

01:09:20.010 --> 01:09:22.230
Don't leave me alone.

01:09:22.810 --> 01:09:26.550
Stay by me. By my side.

01:09:26.810 --> 01:09:30.050
Hold this hand...

01:09:39.130 --> 01:09:40.930
K-Kondo?!

01:09:41.000 --> 01:09:42.510
What are you doing?

01:09:43.110 --> 01:09:46.510
Do you know what you're
doing right now?!

01:09:46.540 --> 01:09:49.350
I'm the traitor who tried to kill you.

01:09:51.020 --> 01:09:54.580
The boss is at fault if there's a revolt.

01:09:55.040 --> 01:09:59.040
Soldiers will lose their lives if they
stay with an incompetent general.

01:09:59.040 --> 01:10:00.890
They're not at fault for killing him.

01:10:01.270 --> 01:10:06.060
Sorry. I'm not a good enough
general to be your superior.

01:10:07.560 --> 01:10:09.770
I was never suited to be the boss.

01:10:09.770 --> 01:10:14.080
You're far more suited to be the boss.

01:10:14.740 --> 01:10:18.350
I can't stand by while squad
members are dying.

01:10:18.500 --> 01:10:21.120
I can't ever use suicide squads.

01:10:21.120 --> 01:10:26.690
Sensei, I'm not a soldier.

01:10:27.020 --> 01:10:33.610
But I wanted you to be by my side as
a friend that I would pour drinks with.

01:10:33.610 --> 01:10:39.450
There were still so many things I wanted
you to teach me, Sensei...

01:10:39.770 --> 01:10:44.330
It's not my fault I'm alone! I'm not at fault!

01:10:44.640 --> 01:10:47.920
They're incompetent!
They're completely incompetent!

01:10:48.690 --> 01:10:53.940
We live in different worlds.
I was a chosen individual.

01:10:54.570 --> 01:10:58.940
I couldn't accept my loneliness and
I blamed my loneliness on others.

01:10:59.460 --> 01:11:02.950
I was afraid that people would
reject me, so I rejected them.

01:11:03.620 --> 01:11:07.250
I was afraid I would get hurt, so
I acted as if I liked being alone.

01:11:08.050 --> 01:11:10.040
I built a wall around my heart.

01:11:11.140 --> 01:11:15.590
But my lingering desire for attention
grew stronger by the day.

01:11:15.970 --> 01:11:18.190
I wanted to be accepted by others.

01:11:18.190 --> 01:11:20.430
Even when I was accepted,
I wasn't satisfied.

01:11:20.430 --> 01:11:23.260
I could do better. I'm not like them.

01:11:23.570 --> 01:11:26.900
I'll show them who I am.

01:11:27.190 --> 01:11:32.660
You don't want someone who
understands and accepts you.

01:11:32.980 --> 01:11:35.120
I had forgotten what I really wanted.

01:11:35.450 --> 01:11:44.420
It wasn't power, fame, military exploits, talent,
or someone who understood me.

01:11:45.130 --> 01:11:49.350
I just wanted someone to be by my side.

01:11:49.550 --> 01:11:52.650
I just wanted someone to see me.

01:11:53.320 --> 01:11:56.320
I just didn't want to be alone anymore.

01:11:59.040 --> 01:12:00.830
I just wanted...

01:12:02.700 --> 01:12:04.630
Sensei!

01:12:07.590 --> 01:12:10.200
Friends who would accept
me for who I was.

01:12:11.910 --> 01:12:13.710
Hey, look over there!

01:12:13.710 --> 01:12:15.040
What are you doing?!

01:12:15.910 --> 01:12:17.980
Hurry up and run away!

01:12:20.880 --> 01:12:23.530
Someone who would
look directly at me...

01:12:25.270 --> 01:12:27.510
Someday, I'll kill you.

01:12:30.650 --> 01:12:33.000
And take me head on.

01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:34.230
I just...

01:12:34.820 --> 01:12:36.740
Wanted friends.

01:12:37.170 --> 01:12:39.240
The thing I wanted...

01:12:40.010 --> 01:12:41.800
Was something...

01:12:41.800 --> 01:12:44.030
I already had.

01:12:46.640 --> 01:12:50.750
Hijikata-kun, I have something
I want to say to you.

01:12:50.930 --> 01:12:53.750
What a coincidence. Me, too.

01:12:54.390 --> 01:12:56.620
I hate you.

01:12:56.620 --> 01:12:59.590
Someday, I'll kill you. So...

01:13:00.050 --> 01:13:02.330
Don't die here.

01:13:02.810 --> 01:13:05.440
The bond I wanted so much...

01:13:05.750 --> 01:13:08.180
Was right here all along.

01:13:30.200 --> 01:13:32.400
I can't see your swings or your rhythm!

01:13:32.650 --> 01:13:34.720
Out of the way, damn it!!

01:13:39.950 --> 01:13:41.890
Don't you understand that...

01:13:41.890 --> 01:13:43.970
I'm telling you to get out of my way?!

01:13:44.090 --> 01:13:46.510
I don't have the time

01:13:46.510 --> 01:13:47.700
to deal with...

01:13:47.700 --> 01:13:48.830
idiots like you!

01:13:52.960 --> 01:13:54.650
Strings?!

01:13:54.050 --> 01:13:58.270
You shouldn't push yourself.
Your arms and legs will rip off.

01:13:58.270 --> 01:14:01.780
Even if you go to help
them now, it's too late.

01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:04.750
Do you think your friends are still alive?

01:14:04.960 --> 01:14:08.550
Even if they survived that explosion...

01:14:08.550 --> 01:14:11.250
We've taken many measures.

01:14:11.660 --> 01:14:14.160
The Shinsengumi will disappear.

01:14:15.610 --> 01:14:18.530
I told you that your arms
and legs will rip off.

01:14:19.370 --> 01:14:22.660
Who'd want to go and save their sorry asses?

01:14:24.870 --> 01:14:29.170
I can't stop. My body won't listen to me.

01:14:29.540 --> 01:14:32.220
It's being pulled forward.

01:14:32.390 --> 01:14:36.240
Strings are pulling me from
the front and the back.

01:14:36.620 --> 01:14:40.680
It annoys me to no end...

01:14:42.410 --> 01:14:44.890
These strings are as strong
as steel, but still...

01:14:45.090 --> 01:14:48.580
You can have an arm and a leg or two...

01:14:48.890 --> 01:14:51.990
Even if these strings can cut flesh...

01:14:51.990 --> 01:14:53.000
I'd like to see them

01:14:53.000 --> 01:14:54.460
try to sever

01:14:54.460 --> 01:14:57.790
an obnoxious bond!

01:15:06.300 --> 01:15:08.110
Get down!

01:15:31.570 --> 01:15:34.090
Sensei!

01:15:31.570 --> 01:15:33.060
Ito!

01:15:41.530 --> 01:15:44.360
Ito!

01:15:52.480 --> 01:15:54.160
Gin-san!

01:15:56.950 --> 01:15:59.250
Bansai-sama... In front!

01:16:06.690 --> 01:16:10.110
Shiroyasha! What is it you fight for?

01:16:10.110 --> 01:16:12.660
What is it you risk your life for?!

01:16:12.660 --> 01:16:15.090
The destruction of the samurai's
world is already inevitable.

01:16:15.090 --> 01:16:19.050
Even if Shinsuke does not soil his
hands, this country will rot away!

01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:21.470
Your struggles alone will not stop it!

01:16:21.470 --> 01:16:24.170
There's no longer anything worth
saving of this country!

01:16:24.170 --> 01:16:25.790
It's the samurai's duty to graciously give

01:16:25.790 --> 01:16:29.720
this rotting country which has been completely
ravaged by the Amanto it's final rites!

01:16:29.720 --> 01:16:32.030
This country must slit its belly!

01:16:32.030 --> 01:16:35.760
If you want to die, then go ahead
and kill yourself with the coals!

01:16:32.030 --> 01:16:35.760
[Note: Coal briquettes are often used for
suicide by carbon monoxide poisoning.]

01:16:35.760 --> 01:16:39.490
Gintoki Sakata...you are a ghost.

01:16:39.490 --> 01:16:45.300
You once tried to protect this country
along with Shinsuke and the others.

01:16:45.300 --> 01:16:52.640
You are obsessed and unable to
let go. You are a living ghost.

01:16:53.720 --> 01:16:57.840
There is no longer anything
for you to protect!

01:16:57.840 --> 01:17:00.850
Ghosts should go back
where they belong.

01:17:07.960 --> 01:17:10.460
I'll play you a requiem!

01:17:15.490 --> 01:17:16.900
The strings...!

01:17:20.470 --> 01:17:21.930
Hey, buddy!

01:17:22.540 --> 01:17:24.910
Take off those headphones, dammit!

01:17:25.260 --> 01:17:27.430
When did he grab my strings?

01:17:27.430 --> 01:17:28.810
What're your waiting for? Fire!

01:17:31.480 --> 01:17:34.800
Clean out your ears and listen up!

01:17:34.800 --> 01:17:39.520
I've never once fought for the
sake of this cheap country.

01:17:40.240 --> 01:17:41.480
I couldn't care less...

01:17:41.480 --> 01:17:45.460
if the country or samurai
fell. I have always...

01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:51.260
Then, and now... What I protect...

01:17:54.390 --> 01:17:56.740
has never changed!

01:18:08.990 --> 01:18:11.020
Bansai-sama!

01:18:14.850 --> 01:18:16.950
What're you doing?

01:18:18.570 --> 01:18:20.900
Get your heads out of your asses!

01:18:22.720 --> 01:18:24.210
Vice-Chief...

01:18:24.210 --> 01:18:26.230
...your orders...

01:18:30.850 --> 01:18:35.360
This is to all of you! I've taken their leader's head!

01:18:35.360 --> 01:18:38.330
The enemy is nothing more
than a flock of lost sheep!

01:18:38.330 --> 01:18:40.830
Finish them off all at once!

01:19:00.620 --> 01:19:02.720
Tsk, retreat!

01:19:04.520 --> 01:19:07.980
Don't let them get away! Kill them all!

01:19:19.410 --> 01:19:22.770
Why...why did you do that?

01:19:24.190 --> 01:19:28.880
You committed treason.
Why did you protect us?

01:19:29.800 --> 01:19:33.680
You're...not Shinsengumi...

01:19:34.280 --> 01:19:40.280
but you seem to be tied to them in
a way that words cannot describe.

01:19:41.210 --> 01:19:45.210
You're neither friends,
nor are you enemies.

01:19:46.430 --> 01:19:48.450
...we're obnoxious bonds.

01:19:48.450 --> 01:19:53.300
Hmph, I suppose there
are ties like that...

01:19:53.300 --> 01:19:59.240
I didn't know. Or rather, I
didn't try to understand.

01:19:59.810 --> 01:20:06.090
Despite hoping to create ties with people,
I severed them on my side.

01:20:06.950 --> 01:20:14.220
I lost sight of what I really wanted because
I tried to protect a tiny bit of pride.

01:20:15.270 --> 01:20:18.250
Even when I finally found the ties
that were important to me,

01:20:18.250 --> 01:20:21.050
I destroyed them on my side.

01:20:22.500 --> 01:20:24.170
Why...

01:20:25.190 --> 01:20:30.500
Why is it always too late when
you finally realize that?

01:20:31.870 --> 01:20:35.360
Why is that I want to fight with everyone
but I can't even stand?

01:20:36.920 --> 01:20:40.360
Why is that I want to wield my
sword, but I have no arm?

01:20:42.250 --> 01:20:49.220
Why is it that...I finally truly realized
that...but I'm going to die...?

01:20:51.080 --> 01:20:57.710
I don't want to die. If I die, I'll be
alone...no ties would reach me...

01:21:00.890 --> 01:21:04.370
I don't want to be alone anymore...

01:21:06.170 --> 01:21:08.420
We'd like you to...

01:21:08.420 --> 01:21:10.220
hand him over to us.

01:21:11.000 --> 01:21:13.980
...Please. He's gone through enough.

01:21:15.220 --> 01:21:18.900
Odd Jobs... We owe you
for your help this time.

01:21:18.900 --> 01:21:21.730
But we cannot heed your request.

01:21:21.730 --> 01:21:25.600
How many people do you think
lost their lives because of him?

01:21:25.600 --> 01:21:29.110
We must deal with the traitor ourselves.

01:21:29.490 --> 01:21:32.170
He saved us! And he...

01:21:33.140 --> 01:21:34.630
Kondo-san!

01:21:34.630 --> 01:21:36.230
Take him.

01:21:36.950 --> 01:21:38.440
Why?!

01:21:42.370 --> 01:21:44.600
Kondo-san, why...?

01:21:46.190 --> 01:21:47.870
Kondo-san...

01:21:56.270 --> 01:22:00.460
That's right...he'd die anyway
even if they left him alone.

01:22:02.320 --> 01:22:04.010
That's exactly why...

01:22:06.440 --> 01:22:09.410
That's exactly why they must kill him.

01:22:22.220 --> 01:22:24.440
Get up...Ito.

01:22:28.300 --> 01:22:30.800
What do you say we settle this?

01:22:31.640 --> 01:22:37.670
They...don't want him to die
a filthy traitor's death.

01:22:38.700 --> 01:22:42.140
They want him to end his
life...as a samurai...

01:22:52.460 --> 01:22:54.320
...and a fellow comrade.

01:22:54.320 --> 01:22:57.640
That's the death he deserves.

01:23:13.010 --> 01:23:15.010
Hijikata!

01:23:15.010 --> 01:23:17.260
Ito!

01:24:04.550 --> 01:24:07.940
...ank...you...

01:24:11.460 --> 01:24:13.900
Thank...you...

01:24:48.150 --> 01:24:53.240
I see. Ito died and the
Shinsengumi survived.

01:24:53.840 --> 01:24:57.900
So the Bakufu is unexpectedly
alive and well.

01:24:58.960 --> 01:25:01.800
No, perhaps Ito was weak...or...

01:25:02.880 --> 01:25:07.230
Was it you who was weak, Bansai?

01:25:07.630 --> 01:25:09.960
The original intent of this job

01:25:09.960 --> 01:25:13.940
was to draw away the Shinsengumi's
attention from the Bakufu bigwigs.

01:25:14.630 --> 01:25:16.720
If the Harusame successfully
made their secret voyage

01:25:16.720 --> 01:25:21.050
and a secret agreement was reached with the Bakufu
bigwigs, there's no need for a battle.

01:25:21.050 --> 01:25:23.380
We would have succeeded
in warding them off.

01:25:24.100 --> 01:25:28.750
I thought I told you to handle this with
the intent of crushing the Shinsengumi.

01:25:28.750 --> 01:25:32.480
As in all things, it's all about
the beat and the timing.

01:25:32.480 --> 01:25:35.350
Without both, nothing will go well.

01:25:35.350 --> 01:25:39.260
If I can't get into it, I back out
immediately. That's how I do things.

01:25:39.870 --> 01:25:41.540
Bansai.

01:25:41.540 --> 01:25:43.490
You can't get attuned my song?

01:25:44.830 --> 01:25:50.550
The Shiroyasha said, "What I protect has never changed."

01:25:51.440 --> 01:25:54.340
Shinsuke...any idea what he was talking about?

01:25:56.160 --> 01:25:59.630
It made me feel like asking him until I find out.

01:26:00.040 --> 01:26:04.230
I've fallen in love with their song. I've lost.

01:26:37.370 --> 01:26:38.750
...This is bad...

01:26:39.580 --> 01:26:43.950
Really bad. They totally think I'm dead.

01:26:43.950 --> 01:26:46.970
I never dreamed they would
hold a funeral so soon.

01:26:46.970 --> 01:26:49.590
I'm totally too late. I blew the timing.

01:26:55.300 --> 01:26:57.460
...I've changed my mind.

01:26:58.510 --> 01:27:02.050
I want to hear...a bit more of your song.

01:27:05.320 --> 01:27:10.630
Live on, I look forward to the day when
you'll let me hear the rest of it.

01:27:11.150 --> 01:27:13.270
And so that's how it went.

01:27:13.270 --> 01:27:16.340
No one expected that I would
miraculously still be alive.

01:27:16.340 --> 01:27:18.010
This is bad.

01:27:18.010 --> 01:27:20.170
Not only was I spared because
of the enemy's compassion,

01:27:20.170 --> 01:27:23.590
but if they found out I spent all this time
in the hospital without contacting them...

01:27:23.590 --> 01:27:25.930
And the timing couldn't be worse.

01:27:25.930 --> 01:27:28.280
"Sorry, I'm alive, after all."

01:27:28.280 --> 01:27:31.830
If I showed up like that, they'd
discipline me...for sure.

01:27:31.830 --> 01:27:33.850
I'm in big trouble. What'll I do?!

01:27:33.850 --> 01:27:36.340
Maybe I should die. At this point, things
would be easier if I were dead.

01:27:36.340 --> 01:27:41.530
You fool! Leaving this life before
an old man! You....you...you...!

01:27:41.530 --> 01:27:44.200
Stop it! Don't make it any worse!

01:27:44.200 --> 01:27:45.980
You're making it harder and
harder for me to show myself.

01:27:45.980 --> 01:27:51.790
You know I...thought of
you...like a real son...

01:27:51.790 --> 01:27:52.720
I didn't know...

01:27:52.720 --> 01:27:55.720
...Pops...that you thought
so highly of me...

01:27:55.720 --> 01:27:58.970
Pusuke! Don't leave me behind!

01:27:58.970 --> 01:28:02.000
Why am I alongside a dog?!

01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:05.920
Or rather...this funeral is
totally about the dog!

01:28:05.920 --> 01:28:09.510
It's like, "we may as well include
Yamazaki while we're at it!"

01:28:09.510 --> 01:28:12.650
Regardless of how unremarkable
I may have been, this is too cruel!

01:28:12.650 --> 01:28:17.080
Why is there a can of Nilo
there as an offering?!

01:28:12.650 --> 01:28:17.080
[Note: Parody of Milo, the Nestle chocolate drink.]

01:28:17.630 --> 01:28:21.620
Hey Priest! Why're you
sipping on my Nilo?!

01:28:21.620 --> 01:28:23.590
Not that I really cared for it
or anything, but cut it out!

01:28:23.590 --> 01:28:24.610
You're making me angry.

01:28:24.610 --> 01:28:26.620
Hey! Turn off that cell phone.

01:28:26.620 --> 01:28:30.800
Huh? I'm at the funeral for
Boss Matsudaira's dog.

01:28:30.800 --> 01:28:32.750
Tell them it's my funeral.

01:28:32.750 --> 01:28:33.700
Oww...

01:28:33.700 --> 01:28:35.180
My leg fell asleep.

01:28:35.180 --> 01:28:37.240
Put away the JUMP, dammit.

01:28:37.240 --> 01:28:39.910
Doesn't a human life mean
anything to you?

01:28:39.910 --> 01:28:43.130
How could they! They're like an
undisciplined gang of hoodlums.

01:28:43.130 --> 01:28:45.710
The Vice-Chief...isn't the
Vice-Chief back yet?

01:28:45.710 --> 01:28:49.670
What's with this? Haven't they
lifted Vice-Chief's punishment?

01:28:49.670 --> 01:28:53.090
Without his leadership, the Shinsengumi
wouldn't exist today.

01:28:53.090 --> 01:28:57.560
Seems he feels personally
responsible this time.

01:28:57.560 --> 01:29:00.390
I heard he personally asked for
the suspension to be extended.

01:29:00.960 --> 01:29:05.510
we may not be able to return to the
Shinsengumi we were before.

01:29:08.110 --> 01:29:09.660
Thank you for waiting.

01:29:10.960 --> 01:29:13.760
I visited every temple
and shrine in the city

01:29:13.760 --> 01:29:16.760
and had them do every incantation
and prayer they knew.

01:29:16.760 --> 01:29:20.190
But in the end, this never left my side.

01:29:20.190 --> 01:29:25.770
Seems this thing's curse...is deeply
ingrained in my very being.

01:29:25.770 --> 01:29:29.510
No telling when this will
consume me again.

01:29:29.510 --> 01:29:31.390
Does that mean you won't return
to the Shinsengumi?

01:29:31.390 --> 01:29:33.900
You should think about changing jobs.

01:29:33.900 --> 01:29:36.120
Maybe you should join Animate.

01:29:33.900 --> 01:29:38.350
[Note: Animate is a chain that sells
everything related to animation.]

01:29:36.120 --> 01:29:38.350
Sounds good to me.

01:29:39.490 --> 01:29:41.920
A demonic sword that never
leaves your side.

01:29:41.920 --> 01:29:47.320
You are truly one with your sword.
It's the perfect sword for you.

01:29:48.230 --> 01:29:51.380
You are the soul of the Shinsengumi.

01:29:51.380 --> 01:29:53.570
We are the sword that protects you.

01:29:58.870 --> 01:30:00.940
You say that so casually.

01:30:02.500 --> 01:30:03.990
Thanks for you help.

01:30:03.990 --> 01:30:05.680
Hijikata-san, where are you going?

01:30:05.680 --> 01:30:07.730
Isn't it obvious?

01:30:08.420 --> 01:30:12.800
My body has more angry spirits and curses
on it than it can accommodate.

01:30:12.800 --> 01:30:16.530
It's full of all the people I've stepped
over and the enmity of my comrades.

01:30:17.020 --> 01:30:21.320
What's another curse or two gonna do?

01:30:21.320 --> 01:30:24.050
I don't intend to look back
no matter who dies.

01:30:25.970 --> 01:30:28.650
I intend to shoulder every one
of them and move forward...

01:30:29.220 --> 01:30:32.190
so they won't laugh at me in Hell.

01:30:37.280 --> 01:30:39.390
...Nice weather.

01:30:39.390 --> 01:30:40.170
Oh.

01:30:40.170 --> 01:30:42.260
We forgot to collect our fee.

01:30:42.260 --> 01:30:43.610
Forget it.

01:30:43.610 --> 01:30:47.740
It's better to collect a little at a
time rather than all at once.

01:30:48.240 --> 01:30:50.340
Do you think he'll be okay, though?

01:30:50.340 --> 01:30:52.220
Will he be able to continue working?

01:30:52.220 --> 01:30:53.430
He'll be fine.

01:30:54.630 --> 01:30:56.780
We don't have to worry any more.

01:30:59.600 --> 01:31:05.090
Oh yeah, here we go!

01:31:13.680 --> 01:31:17.720
They don't give a shit!
What do they think a funeral is?!

01:31:17.720 --> 01:31:20.220
I'll show all of you!
You all should be punished!

01:31:21.150 --> 01:31:24.590
I'll scare the hell out of all of you and...

01:31:30.420 --> 01:31:32.810
Yamazaki returned from the dead!

01:31:32.810 --> 01:31:34.590
Rule No. 22.

01:31:35.500 --> 01:31:39.810
No reading of manga, except for MAGAZINE,
allowed in the headquarters.

01:31:35.500 --> 01:31:39.810
[Note: Refers to "Weekly Shonen MAGAZINE,
a rival of Shonen JUMP.]

01:31:40.670 --> 01:31:42.910
Rule No. 17.

01:31:42.910 --> 01:31:48.080
Turn off cell phones during meetings
and important ceremonies.

01:31:48.700 --> 01:31:51.580
Rule No. 45.

01:31:51.880 --> 01:31:54.320
Do not die and return from the dead.

01:31:55.130 --> 01:31:58.370
Samurai should rest in peace
with good grace.

01:31:58.920 --> 01:32:02.930
The entire lot of you are breaking the
Bushido principles! Slit your bellies!

01:32:02.930 --> 01:32:04.740
Vice-Chief...

01:32:06.310 --> 01:32:07.930
Vice-Chief!

01:32:07.930 --> 01:32:08.700
Ouch.

01:32:09.030 --> 01:32:12.070
Hooray! The Vice-Chief came back!

01:32:12.070 --> 01:32:13.940
What're you guys talking about?

01:32:13.940 --> 01:32:15.000
I said you all have to slit your bellies!

01:32:15.000 --> 01:32:18.460
Oh, we will. We'll do it as
many times as you want.

01:32:20.920 --> 01:32:26.140
Toshi... You said I was the
soul of the Shinsengumi.

01:32:26.650 --> 01:32:31.260
But to these guys, you're also an
irreplaceable part of that soul.

01:32:32.860 --> 01:32:36.270
Good to have you back...Toshi.

01:32:46.320 --> 01:32:50.160
Hello. Hijikata speaking de gozaru.
